ize:10.0pt">The risk reduction model in IEC 61508 ed2.0 comprises the risk reduction arising from the &#8220;E/E/PE safety-related systems&#8221; and &#8220;other risk reduction measures&#8221;. In IEC 61508 ed1.0 the terms &#8220;\other technology safety related systems&#8221; and &#8220;external risk reduction facilities&#8221; were used to encompass what is now referred to as &#8220;other risk reduction measures&#8221;. There are no changes of principle; the changes are essential\ly simplifications to the overall risk model and changes in terminology; see Figure 2 of IEC 61508-1.</span></p></body>)/Rect[155.703 709.821 181.577 723.906]/Subj(Highlight)/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj104 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 103 0 R/Rect[595.22 603.492 775.22 723.492]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj105 0 obj<</AP<</N 7264 0 R>>/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/Contents(\(14\) This new text has been added to in consideration of the security issues; see 1 m\) and 7.4.2.5 of IEC 61508-1.)/CreationDate(D:20100523170638+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20100523170642+02'00')/NM(b769311f-e59f-405f-b3a3-a61b8d802474)/P 100 0 R/Popup 106 0 R/QuadPoints[466.083 493.088 484.873 493.088 466.083 479.831 484.873 479.831]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">\(14\) </span><span\ dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt">This new text has been added to in consideration of the security issues; see 1 m\) and 7.4.2.5 of IEC 61508-1.</span></p></body>)/Rect[462.544 479.417 488.412 493.502]/Subj(Highlight)/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj106 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 105 0 R/Rect[595.22 373.088 775.22 493.088]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj107 0 obj<</AP<</N 7269 0 R>>/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/Contents(\(15\) This new text has been added in consideration of the security issues; see 1 k\) and 7.4.2.5 of IEC 61508-1.)/CreationDate(D:20100523170716+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20100523170720+02'00')/NM(70987952-afb1-46a7-a4d7-7112d43f1098)/P 100 0 R/Popup 108 0 R/QuadPoints[363.725 395.279 382.515 395.279 363.725 382.023 382.515 382.023]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">\(15\) </span><span\ dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt">This new text has been added in consideration of the security issues; see 1 k\) and 7.4.2.5 of IEC 61508-1.</span></p></body>)/Rect[360.186 381.608 386.054 395.694]/Subj(Highlight)/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj108 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 107 0 R/Rect[595.22 275.279 775.22 395.279]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj109 0 obj<</AP<</N 7271 0 R>>/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/Contents(\(16\) IEC 61508 is a Standard that can be used for any application but it is also intended to be used by IEC technical committees as a basis for the development of Standards covering different sectors and products where functional safety of electrical/el\ectronic/programmable electronic systems are within the scope of the Standard. In this latter role, IEC 61508-1/2/3/4 has the status of a basic safety publication and technical committees are obliged to use the principles and requirements in IEC 61508 whe\n developing sector or product Standards where functional safety of electrical/electronic/programmable electronic systems are within the scope of the Standard. However, the basic safety publication status with respect to IEC 61508-1/2/3/4 does not apply i\n the case of medical equipment in compliance with the IEC 60601 series.)/CreationDate(D:20100523170756+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20100524172051+02'00')/NM(d2fcb84f-7863-4e6d-96b9-b825851a5213)/P 100 0 R/Popup 110 0 R/QuadPoints[463.454 378.835 482.244 378.835 463.454 365.579 482.244 365.579]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">\(16\) </span><span\ dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt">IEC 61508 is a Standard that can be used for any application but it is also intended to be used by IEC technical committees as a basis for the development of Standards covering different sectors and products where funct\ional safety of electrical/electronic/programmable electronic systems are within the scope of the Standard. In this latter role, IEC 61508-1/2/3/4 has the status of a basic safety publication and technical committees are obliged to use the principles and \requirements in IEC 61508 when developing sector or product Standards where functional safety of electrical/electronic/programmable electronic systems are within the scope of the Standard. However, the basic safety publication status with respect to IEC 6\1508-1/2/3/4 does not apply in the case of medical equipment in compliance with the IEC 60601 series.</span></p></body>)/Rect[459.915 365.164 485.783 379.25]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj110 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 109 0 R/Rect[595.22 258.835 775.22 378.835]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj111 0 obj<</AP<</N 7276 0 R>>/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/Contents(\(16\) IEC 61508 is a Standard that can be used for any application but it is also intended to be used by IEC technical committees as a basis for the development of Standards covering different sectors and products where functional safety of electrical/el\ectronic/programmable electronic systems are within the scope of the Standard. In this latter role, IEC 61508-1/2/3/4 has the status of a basic safety publication and technical committees are obliged to use the principles and requirements in IEC 61508 whe\n developing sector or product Standards where functional safety of electrical/electronic/programmable electronic systems are within the scope of the Standard. However, the basic safety publication status with respect to IEC 61508-1/2/3/4 does not apply i\n the case of medical equipment in compliance with the IEC 60601 series.)/CreationDate(D:20100523170810+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20100524172051+02'00')/NM(0fd0bdf3-058c-41c1-a6dc-6dc79bc4eac0)/P 100 0 R/Popup 112 0 R/QuadPoints[174.116 122.399 192.906 122.399 174.116 109.142 192.906 109.142]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">\(16\) </span><span\ dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt">IEC 61508 is a Standard that can be used for any application but it is also intended to be used by IEC technical committees as a basis for the development of Standards covering different sectors and products where funct\ional safety of electrical/electronic/programmable electronic systems are within the scope of the Standard. In this latter role, IEC 61508-1/2/3/4 has the status of a basic safety publication and technical committees are obliged to use the principles and \requirements in IEC 61508 when developing sector or product Standards where functional safety of electrical/electronic/programmable electronic systems are within the scope of the Standard. However, the basic safety publication status with respect to IEC 6\1508-1/2/3/4 does not apply in the case of medical equipment in compliance with the IEC 60601 series.</span></p></body>)/Rect[170.577 108.728 196.446 122.813]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj112 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 111 0 R/Rect[595.22 2.39902 775.22 122.399]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj113 0 obj<</AP<</N 7279 0 R>>/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/Contents(\(17\) The original Note is no longer relevant since the proposed process sector implementation of IEC 61508 has been published in the USA and Canada \(i.e. IEC 61511\).)/CreationDate(D:20100523170949+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20100524172051+02'00')/NM(86b8067e-4069-408b-bacc-7ac795f7942c)/P 100 0 R/Popup 114 0 R/QuadPoints[70.9193 68.1705 86.1959 68.1705 70.9193 57.4694 86.1959 57.4694]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">\(17\) </span><span\ dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt">The original Note is no longer relevant since the proposed process sector implementation of IEC 61508 has been published in the USA and Canada \(i.e. IEC 61511\).</span></p></body>)/Rect[68.0625 57.1348 89.0527 68.5051]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj114 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 113 0 R/Rect[595.22 -51.8295 775.22 68.1705]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj115 0 obj<</Filter/FlateDecode/Length 5415>>stream
