inology; see Table 1 and 3.2.13 of IEC 61508-4.</span></p></body>)/Rect[396.746 234.013 412.932 245.383]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj324 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 323 0 R/Rect[595.22 125.049 775.22 245.049]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj325 0 obj<</AP<</N 7413 0 R>>/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/Contents(\(1\) The term "element" although used extensively in IEC 61508 ed1.0 was not a defined term. The term has now been defined in 3.4.5 of IEC 61508-4 ed2.0.)/CreationDate(D:20100523155536+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20100524172124+02'00')/NM(62054f79-420e-4166-84e8-280da0d1001e)/P 320 0 R/Popup 326 0 R/QuadPoints[224.758 130.809 235.231 130.809 224.758 120.107 235.231 120.107]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">\(1\)</span><span d\ir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt"> The term &quot;element&quot; although used extensively in IEC 61508 ed1.0 was not a defined term. The term has now been defined in 3.4.5 of IEC 61508-4 ed2.0.</span></p></body>)/Rect[221.901 119.773 238.088 131.143]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj326 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 325 0 R/Rect[595.22 10.8085 775.22 130.809]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj327 0 obj<</AP<</N 7416 0 R>>/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/Contents(\(40\) The Overall Safety Lifecycle has been modified to take into account that:\ra\) In IEC 61508 ed1.0 there was only one specification covering the safety requirements for an E/E/PE safety-related system \(i.e. the E/E/PES safety requirements specifica\tion\). IEC 61508 ed2.0 now has two specifications: \rthe E/E/PE system safety requirements specification; see 7.10 and Figure 2 of IEC 61508-1 ed2.0; and\rthe E/E/PE system design requirements specification; see 7.10 and Figure 3 of IEC 61508-2 ed2.0.\rb\\) The change to the overall risk reduction model used in IEC 61508 ed2.0 has led to the merging of Boxes 10 and 11 in Figure 2 of IEC 61508-1 ed1.0 into a single Box 11 in Figure 2 of IEC 61508-1 ed2.0; see also Explanation 13.)/CreationDate(D:20100523171936+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20100524172137+02'00')/NM(ec14df9e-9ee8-4a95-9125-a22b79cbe34f)/P 320 0 R/Popup 328 0 R/QuadPoints[374.397 111.26 393.187 111.26 374.397 98.0033 393.187 98.0033]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">\(40\) </span><span\ dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt">The Overall Safety Lifecycle has been modified to take into account that:&#13;a\) In IEC 61508 ed1.0 there was only one specification covering the safety requirements for an E/E/PE safety-related system \(i.e. the E/E/P\ES safety requirements specification\). IEC 61508 ed2.0 now has two specifications: &#13;the E/E/PE system safety requirements specification; see 7.10 and Figure 2 of IEC 61508-1 ed2.0; and&#13;the E/E/PE system design requirements specification; see 7.10\ and Figure 3 of IEC 61508-2 ed2.0.&#13;b\) The change to the overall risk reduction model used in IEC 61508 ed2.0 has led to the merging of Boxes 10 and 11 in Figure 2 of IEC 61508-1 ed1.0 into a single Box 11 in Figure 2 of IEC 61508-1 ed2.0; see also E\xplanation 13.</span></p></body>)/Rect[370.857 97.5889 396.726 111.674]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj328 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 327 0 R/Rect[595.22 -8.73996 775.22 111.26]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj329 0 obj<</Filter/FlateDecode/Length 6183>>stream
