rminology; see Figure 2 of \IEC 61508-1.)/CreationDate(D:20100523170337+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20100524172217+02'00')/NM(09ff4ac0-a010-4117-a620-483195571e0e)/P 517 0 R/Popup 525 0 R/QuadPoints[461.76 285.26 480.547 285.26 461.76 272.003 480.547 272.003]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">\(13\) </span><span\ dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt">The risk reduction model in IEC 61508 ed2.0 comprises the risk reduction arising from the &#8220;E/E/PE safety-related systems&#8221; and &#8220;other risk reduction measures&#8221;. In IEC 61508 ed1.0 the terms &#8220;\other technology safety related systems&#8221; and &#8220;external risk reduction facilities&#8221; were used to encompass what is now referred to as &#8220;other risk reduction measures&#8221;. There are no changes of principle; the changes are essential\ly simplifications to the overall risk model and changes in terminology; see Figure 2 of IEC 61508-1.</span></p></body>)/Rect[458.221 271.589 484.086 285.675]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj525 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 524 0 R/Rect[595.22 165.26 775.22 285.26]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj526 0 obj<</AP<</N 7519 0 R>>/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/Contents(\(46\) The word overall" has been added to indicate that the safety functions requirements and the safety integrity requirements are part of the Overall Safety Requirements; see 7.5.2.1 including the Notes of IEC 61508-1 ed2.0.)/CreationDate(D:20100523172517+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20100524172200+02'00')/NM(cb2e8b7b-d8f0-4556-985c-95d334335647)/P 517 0 R/Popup 527 0 R/QuadPoints[331.686 308.056 350.473 308.056 331.686 294.8 350.473 294.8]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p di