he term subsystem, as now defined, will mean that it will only be correct to use the term "subsystem" when know\ledge of the application is known since it will be necessary to have knowledge of the dangerous failure modes associated with the specified safety function.)/CreationDate(D:20100523154306+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20100524172228+02'00')/NM(9714abb7-6b28-4e9c-a0fd-0686ddd66107)/P 669 0 R/Popup 679 0 R/QuadPoints[203.876 686.892 223.751 686.892 203.876 673.635 223.751 673.635]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">\(1A\)</span><span \dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt"> The term &#8220;subsystem&#8221; was not a defined term in IEC 61508 ed1.0. However, it is a defined term in 3.4.4 of IEC 61508-4 ed2.0. The use of the term subsystem, as now defined, will mean that it will only be corr\ect to use the term &quot;subsystem&quot; when knowledge of the application is known since it will be necessary to have knowledge of the dangerous failure modes associated with the specified safety function.</span></p></body>)/Rect[200.337 673.221 227.29 687.306]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj679 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 678 0 R/Rect[595.22 566.892 775.22 686.892]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj680 0 obj<</AP<</N 7593 0 R>>/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/Contents(\(1\) The term "element" although used extensively in IEC 61508 ed1.0 was not a defined term. The term has now been defined in 3.4.5 of IEC 61508-4 ed2.0.)/CreationDate(D:20100523155545+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20100524172228+02'00')/NM(0ee06911-11e8-4e99-aea1-d2acde2ff294)/P 669 0 R/Popup 681 0 R/QuadPoints[282.965 686.892 295.883 686.892 282.965 673.635 295.883 673.635]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">\(1\)</span><span d\ir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt"> The term &quot;element&quot; although used extensively in IEC 61508 ed1.0 was not a defined term. The term has now been defined in 3.4.5 of IEC 61508-4 ed2.0.</span></p></body>)/Rect[279.426 673.221 299.422 687.306]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj681 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 680 0 R/Rect[595.22 566.892 775.22 686.892]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj682 0 obj<</AP<</N 7597 0 R>>/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/Contents(\(4\) The revised wording provides a more precise technical description of the intended requirement.)/CreationDate(D:20100523162124+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20100524172239+02'00')/NM(20a275ed-30f6-4825-bb2f-2e509aed5dae)/P 669 0 R/Popup 683 0 R/QuadPoints[434.041 360.26 446.959 360.26 434.041 347.003 446.959 347.003]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">\(4\)</span><span d\ir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt"> The revised wording provides a more precise technical description of the intended requirement.</span></p></body>)/Rect[430.502 346.589 450.498 360.675]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj683 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 682 0 R/Rect[595.22 240.26 775.22 360.26]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj684 0 obj<</AP<</N 7599 0 R>>/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/Contents(\(4\) The revised wording provides a more precise technical description of the intended requirement.)/CreationDate(D:20100523162133+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20100524172239+02'00')/NM(df78ac44-118a-450d-93c7-3e6958f3b3b4)/P 669 0 R/Popup 685 0 R/QuadPoints[278.763 331.456 291.681 331.456 278.763 318.199 291.681 318.199]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2