rous failure modes associated with the specified safety function.)/CreationDate(D:20100523154318+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20100524172248+02'00')/NM(bd4bc928-c14b-43e7-a032-8f303a6ec8d3)/P 755 0 R/Popup 764 0 R/QuadPoints[329.521 448.58 349.397 448.58 329.521 435.323 349.397 435.323]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">\(1A\)</span><span \dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt"> The term &#8220;subsystem&#8221; was not a defined term in IEC 61508 ed1.0. However, it is a defined term in 3.4.4 of IEC 61508-4 ed2.0. The use of the term subsystem, as now defined, will mean that it will only be corr\ect to use the term &quot;subsystem&quot; when knowledge of the application is known since it will be necessary to have knowledge of the dangerous failure modes associated with the specified safety function.</span></p></body>)/Rect[325.982 434.909 352.936 448.994]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj764 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 763 0 R/Rect[595.22 328.58 775.22 448.58]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj765 0 obj<</AP<</N 7633 0 R>>/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/Contents(\(1A\) The term subsystemŽ was not a defined term in IEC 61508 ed1.0. However, it is a defined term in 3.4.4 of IEC 61508-4 ed2.0. The use of the term subsystem, as now defined, will mean that it will only be correct to use the term "subsystem" when know\ledge of the application is known since it will be necessary to have knowledge of the dangerous failure modes associated with the specified safety function.)/CreationDate(D:20100523154330+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20100524172248+02'00')/NM(91e2c7ad-6173-429c-b6af-2f23114ed904)/P 755 0 R/Popup 766 0 R/QuadPoints[126.835 391.44 146.711 391.44 126.835 378.183 146.711 378.183]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">\(1A\)</span><span \dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt"> The term &#8220;subsystem&#8221; was not a defined term in IEC 61508 ed1.0. However, it is a defined term in 3.4.4 of IEC 61508-4 ed2.0. The use of the term subsystem, as now defined, will mean that it will only be corr\ect to use the term &quot;subsystem&quot; when knowledge of the application is known since it will be necessary to have knowledge of the dangerous failure modes associated with the specified safety function.</span></p></body>)/Rect[123.296 377.768 150.25 391.854]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj766 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 765 0 R/Rect[595.22 271.44 775.22 391.44]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj767 0 obj<</AP<</N 7635 0 R>>/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/Contents(\(13\) The risk reduction model in IEC 61508 ed2.0 comprises the risk reduction arising from the E/E/PE safety-related systemsŽ and other risk reduction measuresŽ. In IEC 61508 ed1.0 the terms other technology safety related systemsŽ and external risk\ reduction facilitiesŽ were used to encompass what is now referred to as other risk reduction measuresŽ. There are no changes of principle; the changes are essentially simplifications to the overall risk model and changes in terminology; see Figure 2 of \IEC 61508-1.)/CreationDate(D:20100523170442+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20100524172248+02'00')/NM(299f7200-a366-4c60-bac3-b2a2e24967b5)/P 755 0 R/Popup 768 0 R/QuadPoints[141.12 130.936 159.922 130.936 141.12 117.679 159.922 117.679]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">\(13\) </span><span\ dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt">The risk reduction model in IEC 61508 ed2.0 comprises the risk reduction arising from the &#8220;E/E/PE safety-related systems&#8221; and &#8220;other risk reduction measures&#8221;. In IEC 61508 ed1.0 the terms &#8220;\other technology safety related systems&#8221; and &#8220;external risk reduction facilities&#8221; were used to encompass what is now referred to as &#8220;other risk reduction measures&#8221;. There are no changes of principle; the changes are essential\ly simplifications to the overall risk model and changes in terminology; see Figure 2 of IEC 61508-1.</span></p></body>)/Rect[137.581 117.265 163.461 131.35]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj768 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 767 0 R/Rect[595.22 10.9358 775.22 130.936]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj769 0 obj<</AP<</N 7638 0 R>>/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/Contents(\(52\) The revised wording provides a more precise technical description of the intended requirement; see 3.1.1 to 3.1.5 of IEC 61508-4 ed2.0 for hazard related definitions and Figure Relationship of hazard related definitionsŽ; click on the paperclip to\ display the Figure.)/CreationDate(D:20100523172847+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20100524172239+02'00')/NM(35870581-f6e8-4373-aaa2-f23935943b26)/P 755 0 R/Popup 770 0 R/QuadPoints[353.424 718.456 372.214 718.456 353.424 705.199 372.214 705.199]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">\(52\) </span><span\ dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt">The revised wording provides a more precise technical description of the intended requirement; see 3.1.1 to 3.1.5 of IEC 61508-4 ed2.0 for hazard related definitions and Figure &#8220;Relationship of hazard related defi\nitions&#8221;;</span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold"> click on the paperclip to display the Figure</span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt">.</span></p></body>)/Rect[349.885 704.785 375.753 718.87]/Subtype/H