bj<</AP<</N 8068 0 R>>/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/Contents(\(1A\) The term subsystemŽ was not a defined term in IEC 61508 ed1.0. However, it is a defined term in 3.4.4 of IEC 61508-4 ed2.0. The use of the term subsystem, as now defined, will mean that it will only be correct to use the term "subsystem" when know\ledge of the application is known since it will be necessary to have knowledge of the dangerous failure modes associated with the specified safety function.)/CreationDate(D:20100523154419+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20100524172423+02'00')/NM(b2bf0d89-ca8a-4e0f-8031-ed29bc7dc128)/P 1791 0 R/Popup 1803 0 R/QuadPoints[479.76 171.26 499.636 171.26 479.76 158.003 499.636 158.003]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">\(1A\)</span><span \dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt"> The term &#8220;subsystem&#8221; was not a defined term in IEC 61508 ed1.0. However, it is a defined term in 3.4.4 of IEC 61508-4 ed2.0. The use of the term subsystem, as now defined, will mean that it will only be corr\ect to use the term &quot;subsystem&quot; when knowledge of the application is known since it will be necessary to have knowledge of the dangerous failure modes associated with the specified safety function.</span></p></body>)/Rect[476.221 157.589 503.175 171.674]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj1803 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 1802 0 R/Rect[595.22 51.26 775.22 171.26]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj1804 0 obj<</AP<</N 8056 0 R>>/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/Contents(\(1\) The term "element" although used extensively in IEC 61508 ed1.0 was not a defined term. The term has now been defined in 3.4.5 of IEC 61508-4 ed2.0.)/CreationDate(D:20100523155734+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20100524172423+02'00')/NM(2c4d02bf-0ddc-4bbf-94b4-30f2d91cd7ce)/P 1791 0 R/Popup 1805 0 R/QuadPoints[117.728 159.736 130.766 159.736 1