/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">\(1A\)</span><span \dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt"> The term &#8220;subsystem&#8221; was not a defined term in IEC 61508 ed1.0. However, it is a defined term in 3.4.4 of IEC 61508-4 ed2.0. The use of the term subsystem, as now defined, will mean that it will only be corr\ect to use the term &quot;subsystem&quot; when knowledge of the application is known since it will be necessary to have knowledge of the dangerous failure modes associated with the specified safety function.</span></p></body>)/Rect[250.745 744.03 277.817 758.115]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj1845 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 1844 0 R/Rect[595.22 637.701 775.22 757.701]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj1846 0 obj<</AP<</N 8096 0 R>>/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/Contents(\(1A\) The term subsystemŽ was not a defined term in IEC 61508 ed1.0. However, it is a defined term in 3.4.4 of IEC 61508-4 ed2.0. The use of the term subsystem, as now defined, will mean that it will only be correct to use the term "subsystem" when know\ledge of the application is known since it will be necessary to have knowledge of the dangerous failure modes associated with the specified safety function.)/CreationDate(D:20100523154433+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20100524172423+02'00')/NM(b881cf22-421d-4963-b2da-358977b63bd4)/P 1838 0 R/Popup 1847 0 R/QuadPoints[458.165 746.177 478.159 746.177 458.165 732.92 478.159 732.92]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">\(1A\)</span><span \dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt"> The term &#8220;subsystem&#8221; was not a defined term in IEC 61508 ed1.0. However, it is a defined term in 3.4.4 of IEC 61508-4 ed2.0. The use of the term subsystem, as now defined, will mean that it 