 now defined, will mean that it will only be corr\ect to use the term &quot;subsystem&quot; when knowledge of the application is known since it will be necessary to have knowledge of the dangerous failure modes associated with the specified safety function.</span></p></body>)/Rect[427.014 717.625 454.087 731.711]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj2320 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 2319 0 R/Rect[595.22 611.297 775.22 731.297]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj2321 0 obj<</AP<</N 8345 0 R>>/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/Contents(\(1\) The term "element" although used extensively in IEC 61508 ed1.0 was not a defined term. The term has now been defined in 3.4.5 of IEC 61508-4 ed2.0.)/CreationDate(D:20100523155927+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20100524172526+02'00')/NM(ce49cd11-94c8-44c1-98dd-824e214448c3)/P 2315 0 R/Popup 2322 0 R/QuadPoints[255.608 524.866 268.646 524.866 255.608 511.609 268.646 511.609]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">\(1\)</span><span d\ir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt"> The term &quot;element&quot; although used extensively in IEC 61508 ed1.0 was not a defined term. The term has now been defined in 3.4.5 of IEC 61508-4 ed2.0.</span></p></body>)/Rect[252.069 511.195 272.185 525.28]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj2322 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 2321 0 R/Rect[595.22 404.866 775.22 524.866]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj2323 0 obj<</AP<</N 8352 0 R>>/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/Contents(\(94\) This is a new requirement; see Explanation 87.)/CreationDate(D:20100523183001+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20100524172526+02'00')/NM(79e137d8-4090-4f25-abaf-4d9320e1e264)/P 2315 0 R/Popup 2324 0 R/QuadPoints[114.236 757.82 133.155 757.82 114.236 744.564 133.155 744.564]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/