pt"> The term &#8220;subsystem&#8221; was not a defined term in IEC 61508 ed1.0. However, it is a defined term in 3.4.4 of IEC 61508-4 ed2.0. The use of the term subsystem, as now defined, will mean that it will only be corr\ect to use the term &quot;subsystem&quot; when knowledge of the application is known since it will be necessary to have knowledge of the dangerous failure modes associated with the specified safety function.</span></p></body>)/Rect[268.738 52.3489 295.811 66.4345]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj2523 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 2522 0 R/Rect[595.22 -53.98 775.22 66.02]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj2524 0 obj<</AP<</N 8469 0 R>>/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/Contents(\(1\) The term "element" although used extensively in IEC 61508 ed1.0 was not a defined term. The term has now been defined in 3.4.5 of IEC 61508-4 ed2.0.)/CreationDate(D:20100523160033+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20100524172553+02'00')/NM(04eeff48-13e9-40fb-994e-03a2b283924c)/P 2516 0 R/Popup 2525 0 R/QuadPoints[182.882 462.376 196.039 462.376 182.882 449.119 196.039 449.119]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">\(1\)</span><span d\ir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt"> The term &quot;element&quot; although used extensively in IEC 61508 ed1.0 was not a defined term. The term has now been defined in 3.4.5 of IEC 61508-4 ed2.0.</span></p></body>)/Rect[179.343 448.705 199.578 462.791]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj2525 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 2524 0 R/Rect[595.22 342.376 775.22 462.376]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj2526 0 obj<</AP<</N 8473 0 R>>/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/Contents(\(1\) The term "element" although used extensively in IEC 61508 ed1.0 was not a defined term. The term has now been defined in 3.4.5 of IEC 61508-4 ed2.0.)/CreationDate(D:20100523160039+02'00')/F 132/M(D:2010052