1508 ed1.0 \(Requirements for E/E/PES implementation\) comprised the requirements for both implementation \(7.4.7.1 to 7.4.7.4\) and proven in use \(7.4.7.1 to 7.4.7.12\). In IEC 61508 ed2.0, these requirements ha\ve been separated into two different subclauses:\rsubclause 7.4.9 Requirements for E/E/PE system implementationŽ, and\rsubclause 7.4.10 Requirements for proven in use elementsŽ.\rThe above two subclauses replace the previous subclause 7.4.7 of IEC 61508\ ed1.0.)/CreationDate(D:20100523183908+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20100524172553+02'00')/NM(afcde9e2-14a1-432b-8e70-d7c3e5d9ac9e)/P 2516 0 R/Popup 2531 0 R/QuadPoints[106.925 610.1 131.726 610.1 106.925 596.843 131.726 596.843]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">\(108\)</span><span\ dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt"> The requirements in 7.4.7 of IEC 61508 ed1.0 \(Requirements for E/E/PES implementation\) comprised the requirements for both implementation \(7.4.7.1 to 7.4.7.4\) and proven in use \(7.4.7.1 to 7.4.7.12\). In IEC 61508\ ed2.0, these requirements have been separated into two different subclauses:&#13;subclause 7.4.9 &#8220;Requirements for E/E/PE system implementation&#8221;, and&#13;subclause 7.4.10 &#8220;Requirements for proven in use elements&#8221;.&#13;The above tw\o subclauses replace the previous subclause 7.4.7 of IEC 61508 ed1.0.</span></p></body>)/Rect[103.386 596.429 135.265 610.514]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj2531 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 2530 0 R/Rect[595.22 490.1 775.22 610.1]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj2532 0 obj<</AP<</N 8481 0 R>>/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/Contents(\(109\) The concept of the safety manual for compliant itemsŽ is a new requirement; see Annex D of IEC 61508-2 ed2.0 and 3.8.17 of IEC 61508-4 ed2.0.)/CreationDate(D:20100523183936+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20