00524172719+02'00')/NM(0fe0cee8-5070-4387-9336-c302fe670a28)/P 3161 0 R/Popup 3170 0 R/QuadPoints[453.362 254.06 466.284 254.06 453.362 240.803 466.284 240.803]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">\(2\) </span><span \dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt">The abbreviation E/E/PESs</span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold"> </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt">\(Electrical/Electronic/Programmable Electronic Systems\)</span><span dir="ltr" s\tyle="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold"> </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt">in IEC 61508 ed1.0 has been changed to</span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold"> </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt">E/E/PE system\ \(Electrical/Electronic/Programmable Electronic system\) in IEC 61508 ed2.0. This is solely a change in terminology; see Table 1 and 3.2.13 of IEC 61508-4.</span></p></body>)/Rect[449.823 240.389 469.823 254.474]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj3170 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 3169 0 R/Rect[595.22 134.06 775.22 254.06]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj3171 0 obj<</AP<</N 8844 0 R>>/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/Contents(\(4\) The revised wording provides a more precise technical description of the intended requirement.)/CreationDate(D:20100523162254+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20100524172709+02'00')/NM(819bf573-79cc-4bab-b41e-dcd362391988)/P 3161 0 R/Popup 3172 0 R/QuadPoints[310.558 555.962 323.589 555.962 310.558 542.705 323.589 542.705]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">\(4\)</span><span d\ir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt"> The revised wording provides a more precise technical description of the intended requirement.</span></p></body>)/Rect[307.019 542.291 327.128 556.376]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj3172 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 3171 0 R/Rect[595.22 435.962 775.22 555.962]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj3173 0 obj<</AP<</N 8845 0 R>>/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/Contents(\(4\) The revised wording provides a more precise technical description of the intended requirement.)/CreationDate(D:20100523162305+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20100524172719+02'00')/NM(60927f98-fced-469a-9fcd-bd852367bf44)/P 3161 0 R/Popup 3174 0 R/QuadPoints[478.551 265.58 491.469 265.58 478.551 252.323 491.469 252.323]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">\(4\)</span><span d\ir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt"> The revised wording provides a more precise technical description of the intended requirement.</span></p></body>)/Rect[475.012 251.909 495.009 265.994]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj3174 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 3173 0 R/Rect[595.22 145.58 775.22 265.58]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj3175 0 obj<</AP<</N 8837 0 R>>/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/Contents(\(16\) IEC 61508 is a Standard that can be used for any application but it is also intended to be used by IEC technical committees as a basis for the development of Standards covering different sectors and products where functional safety of electrical/el\ectronic/programmable electronic systems are within the scope of the Standard. In this latter role, IEC 61508-1/2/3/4 has the status of a basic safety publication and technical committees are obliged to use the principles and requirements in IEC 61508 whe\n developing sector or product Standards where functional safety of electrical/electronic/programmable electronic systems are within the scope of the Standard. However, the basic safety publication status with respect to IEC 61508-1/2/3/4 does not apply i\n the case of medical equipment in compliance with the IEC 60601 series.)/CreationDate(D:20100523170841+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20100524172719+02'00')/NM(a2c034d1-af42-425f-8625-099e69b05cb0)/P 3161 0 R/Popup 3176 0 R/QuadPoints[471.003 111.38 490.042 111.38 471.003 98.1234 490.042 98.1234]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">\(16\) </span><span\ dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt">IEC 61508 is a Standard that can be used for any application but it is also intended to be used by IEC technical committees as a basis for the development of Standards covering different sectors and products where funct\ional safety of electrical/electronic/programmable electronic systems are within the scope of the Standard. In this latter role, IEC 61508-1/2/3/4 has the status of a basic safety publication and technical committees are obliged to use the principles and \requirements in IEC 61508 when developing sector or product Standards where functional safety of electrical/electronic/programmable electronic systems are within the scope of the Standard. However, the basic safety publication status with respect to IEC 6\1508-1/2/3/4 does not apply in the case of medical equipment in compliance with the IEC 60601 series.</span></p></body>)/Rect[467.464 97.709 493.581 111.795]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj3176 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 3175 0 R/Rect[595.22 -8.61987 775.22 111.38]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj3177 0 obj<</AP<</N 8838 0 R>>/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/Contents(\(300\) The change of wording here reflects the additional importance attached to, and additional requirements for, support tools in ed2.0.)/CreationDate(D:20100524135812+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20100524172709+02'00')/NM(a64d169d-5db9-4010-b0bb-f2e17808872d)/P 3161 0 R/Popup 3178 0 R/QuadPoints[88.9194 532.936 113.698 532.936 88.9194 519.68 113.698 519.68]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">\(300\)</span><span\ dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt"> The change of wording here reflects the additional importance attached to, and additional requirements for, support tools in ed2.0.</span></p></body>)/Rect[85.3804 519.265 117.237 533.351]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj3178 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 3177 0 R/Rect[595.22 412.936 775.22 532.936]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj3179 0 obj<</AP<</N 8852 0 R>>/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/Contents(\(300\) The change of wording here reflects the additional importance attached to, and additional requirements for, support tools in ed2.0.)/CreationDate(D:20100524135823+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20100524172719+02'00')/NM(51468638-3fb5-4df3-959e-905653b8f44c)/P 3161 0 R/Popup 3180 0 R/QuadPoints[437.517 477.012 462.424 477.012 437.517 463.756 462.424 463.756]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">\(300\)</span><span\ dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt"> The change of wording here reflects the additional importance attached to, and additional requirements for, support tools in ed2.0.</span></p></body>)/Rect[433.978 463.341 465.964 477.427]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj3180 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 3179 0 R/Rect[595.22 357.012 775.22 477.012]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj3181 0 obj<</AP<</N 8847 0 R>>/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/Contents(\(301\) The term systematic capabilityŽ now replaces safety integrity levelŽ throughout Part 3 \(with a small number of exceptions where the original term is the more appropriate\). This is in recognition of the fact that IEC 61508 can \(in ed2.0\) be a\pplied either to the development of safety related software in a final application system which implements safety functions, or to the development of elements containing software which are intended for use in a safety related system but for which the syst\em design and safety integrity level has not necessarily been determined. Software of systematic capability N \(as created by following the requirements of the Standard\) is capable of being used in a final application system to support a safety function \of SIL N \(or less\), or in some circumstances to support a safety function of SIL N+1 when used in conjunction with other elements.)/CreationDate(D:20100524135901+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20100524172719+02'00')/NM(19f25605-752d-4681-926b-12c2e9bc8690)/P 3161 0 R/Popup 3182 0 R/QuadPoints[192.12 449.056 217.024 449.056 192.12 435.799 217.024 435.799]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">\(301\)</span><span\ dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt"> The term &#8220;systematic capability&#8221; now replaces &#8220;safety integrity level&#8221; throughout Part 3 \(with a small number of exceptions where the original term is the more appropriate\). This is in recogni\tion of the fact that IEC 61508 can \(in ed2.0\) be applied either to the development of safety related software in a final application system which implements safety functions, or to the development of elements containing software which are intended for \use in a safety related system but for which the system design and safety integrity level has not necessarily been determined. Software of systematic capability N \(as created by following the requirements of the Standard\) is capable of being used in a f\inal application system to support a safety function of SIL N \(or less\), or in some circumstances to support a safety function of SIL N+1 when used in conjunction with other elements.</span></p></body>)/Rect[188.581 435.385 220.563 449.47]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj3182 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 3181 0 R/Rect[595.22 329.056 775.22 449.056]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj3183 0 obj<</AP<</N 8857 0 R>>/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/Contents(\(301\) The term systematic capabilityŽ now replaces safety integrity levelŽ throughout Part 3 \(with a small number of exceptions where the original term is the more appropriate\). This is in recognition of the fact that IEC 61508 can \(in ed2.0\) be a\pplied either to the development of safety related software in a final application system which implements safety functions, or to the development of elements containing software which are intended for use in a safety related system but for which the syst\em design and safety integrity level has not necessarily been determined. Software of systematic capability N \(as created by following the requirements of the Standard\) is capable of being used in a final application system to support a safety function \of SIL N \(or less\), or in some circumstances to support a safety function of SIL N+1 when used in conjunction with other elements.)/CreationDate(D:20100524135912+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20100524172719+02'00')/NM(f4f0ccdd-c8b4-4799-b8aa-25f1968c1885)/P 3161 0 R/Popup 3184 0 R/QuadPoints[137.644 282.136 162.563 282.136 137.644 268.88 162.563 268.88]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">\(301\)</span><span\ dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt"> The term &#8220;systematic capability&#8221; now replaces &#8220;safety integrity level&#8221; throughout Part 3 \(with a small number of exceptions where the original term is the more appropriate\). This is in recogni\tion of the fact that IEC 61508 can \(in ed2.0\) be applied either to the development of safety related software in a final application system which implements safety functions, or to the development of elements containing software which are intended for \use in a safety related system but for which the system design and safety integrity level has not necessarily been determined. Software of systematic capability N \(as created by following the requirements of the Standard\) is capable of being used in a f\inal application system to support a safety function of SIL N \(or less\), or in some circumstances to support a safety function of SIL N+1 when used in conjunction with other elements.</span></p></body>)/Rect[134.105 268.465 166.102 282.551]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj3184 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 3183 0 R/Rect[595.22 162.136 775.22 282.136]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj3185 0 obj<</Filter/FlateDecode/Length 5965>>stream
