ion="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">\(4\)</span><span d\ir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt"> The revised wording provides a more precise technical description of the intended requirement.</span></p></body>)/Rect[123.303 533.429 143.299 547.514]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj3232 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 3231 0 R/Rect[595.22 427.1 775.22 547.1]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj3233 0 obj<</AP<</N 8998 0 R>>/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/Contents(\(301\) The term systematic capabilityŽ now replaces safety integrity levelŽ throughout Part 3 \(with a small number of exceptions where the original term is the more appropriate\). This is in recognition of the fact that IEC 61508 can \(in ed2.0\) be a\pplied either to the development of safety related software in a final application system which implements safety functions, or to the development of elements containing software which are intended for use in a safety related system but for which the syst\em design and safety integrity level has not necessarily been determined. Software of systematic capability N \(as created by following the requirements of the Standard\) is capable of being used in a final application system to support a safety function \of SIL N \(or less\), or in some circumstances to support a safety function of SIL N+1 when used in conjunction with other elements.)/CreationDate(D:20100524135921+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20100524172719+02'00')/NM(511aecda-83f2-4eed-930a-51ea8f697d6c)/P 3219 0 R/Popup 3234 0 R/QuadPoints[353.397 746.18 378.3 746.18 353.397 732.923 378.3 732.923]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">\(301\)</span><span\ dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt"> The term &#8220;systematic capability&#8221; now replaces &#8220;safety integrity level&#8221; throughout Part 3 \(with a small number of exceptions where the original term is the more appropriate\). This is in recogni\tion of the fact that IEC 61508 can \(in ed2.0\) be applied either to the development of safety related software in a final application system which implements safety functions, or to the development of elements containing software which are intended for \use in a safety related system but for which the system design and safety integrity level has not necessarily been determined. Software of systematic capability N \(as created by following the requirements of the Standard\) is capable of being used in a f\inal application system to support a safety function of SIL N \(or less\), or in some circumstances to support a safety function of SIL N+1 when used in conjunction with other elements.</span></p></body>)/Rect[349.858 732.509 381.839 746.594]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj3234 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 3233 0 R/Rect[595.22 626.18 775.22 746.18]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj3235 0 obj<</AP<</N 9006 0 R>>/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/Contents(\(302\) The requirement for verification documents has been added to make it clear that evidence resulting from verification methods other than testing must be available.)/CreationDate(D:20100524140111+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20100524172719+02'00')/NM(dac76668-cf78-4b1c-b1e1-ae86c51d8139)/P 3219 0 R/Popup 3236 0 R/QuadPoints[384.246 683.768 409.166 683.768 384.246 670.512 409.166 670.512]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">\(302\) </span><spa\n dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt">The requirement for verification documents has been added to make it clear that evidence resulting from verification methods other than testing must be available.</span></p></body>)/Rect[380.707 670.097 412.705 684.183]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj3236 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 3235 0 R/Rect[595.22 563.768 775.22 683.768]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj3237 0 obj<</AP<</N 9011 0 R>>/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/Contents(\(303\) This subclause has been added to correct an omission of an important activity in ed1.0.)/CreationDate(D:20100524140137+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20100524172728+02'00')/NM(043bc50b-1329-4d48-a537-761ace85436d)/P 3219 0 R/Popup 3238 0 R/QuadPoints[277.202 438.376 302.113 438.376 277.202 425.12 302.113 425.12]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">\(303\)</span><span\ dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt"> This subclause has been added to correct an omission of an important activity in ed1.0.</span></p></body>)/Rect[273.662 424.705 305.652 438.791]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj3238 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 3237 0 R/Rect[595.22 318.376 775.22 438.376]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj3239 0 obj<</Filter/FlateDecode/Length 6509>>stream
