g provides a more precise technical description of the intended requirement.)/CreationDate(D:20100523162356+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20100524172728+02'00')/NM(9324e4b3-2650-4ee6-8446-51cbd7ea4fd3)/P 3246 0 R/Popup 3255 0 R/QuadPoints[493.062 557.78 506.044 557.78 493.062 544.523 506.044 544.523]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">\(4\)</span><span d\ir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt"> The revised wording provides a more precise technical description of the intended requirement.</span></p></body>)/Rect[489.523 544.109 509.583 558.194]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj3255 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 3254 0 R/Rect[595.22 437.78 775.22 557.78]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj3256 0 obj<</AP<</N 9014 0 R>>/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/Contents(\(301\) The term systematic capabilityŽ now replaces safety integrity levelŽ throughout Part 3 \(with a small number of exceptions where the original term is the more appropriate\). This is in recognition of the fact that IEC 61508 can \(in ed2.0\) be a\pplied either to the development of safety related software in a final application system which implements safety functions, or to the development of elements containing software which are intended for use in a safety related system but for which the syst\em design and safety integrity level has not necessarily been determined. Software of systematic capability N \(as created by following the requirements of the Standard\) is capable of being used in a final application system to support a safety function \of SIL N \(or less\), or in some circumstances to support a safety function of SIL N+1 when used in conjunction with other elements.)/CreationDate(D:20100524135929+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20100524172728+02'00')/NM(021f7c3c-ee6f-44ae-a23c-1ea190c0aa24)/P 3246 0 R/Popup 3257 0 R/QuadPoints[146.398 280.445 171.306 280.445 146.398 267.189 171.306 267.189]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">\(301\)</span><span\ dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt"> The term &#8220;systematic capability&#8221; now replaces &#8220;safety integrity level&#8221; throughout Part 3 \(with a small number of exceptions where the original term is the more appropriate\). This is in recogni\tion of the fact that IEC 61508 can \(in ed2.0\) be applied either to the development of safety related software in a final application system which implements safety functions, or to the development of elements containing software which are intended for \use in a safety related system but for which the system design and safety integrity level has not necessarily been determined. Software of systematic capability N \(as created by following the requirements of the Standard\) is capable of being used in a f\inal application system to support a safety function of SIL N \(or less\), or in some circumstances to support a safety function of SIL N+1 when used in conjunction with other elements.</span></p></body>)/Rect[142.859 266.774 174.845 280.86]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj3257 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 3256 0 R/Rect[595.22 160.445 775.22 280.445]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj3258 0 obj<</AP<</N 9018 0 R>>/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/Contents(\(304\) The content of this clause has been moved to 7.1.2.6.)/CreationDate(D:20100524140203+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20100524172728+02'00')/NM(6018d266-d951-4f35-9c2d-9dcf6fe6873a)/P 3246 0 R/Popup 3259 0 R/QuadPoints[244.204 734.656 269.116 734.656 244.204 721.4 269.116 721.4]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">\(304\)</span><span\ dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt"> The content of this clause has been moved to 7.1.2.6.</span></p></body>)/Rect[240.665 720.985 272.655 735.071]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj3259 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 3258 0 R/Rect[595.22 614.656 775.22 734.656]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj3260 0 obj<</AP<</N 9022 0 R>>/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/Contents(\(305\) This clause has been introduced to make it clear that functional safety must still be achieved when an alternative safety lifecycle is selected. The addition of the software properties guidance in Annex C can help in justifying the functional safe\ty of software developed by alternative lifecycle, methods and techniques.)/CreationDate(D:20100524140229+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20100524172728+02'00')/NM(d416f071-e898-4e30-976b-c8c2949ddaa5)/P 3246 0 R/Popup 3261 0 R/QuadPoints[152.996 385.932 178.028 385.932 152.996 372.676 178.028 372.676]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">\(305\) </span><spa\n dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt">This clause has been introduced to make it clear that functional safety must still be achieved when an alternative safety lifecycle is selected. The addition of the software properties guidance in Annex C can help in j\ustifying the functional safety of software developed by alternative lifecycle, methods and techniques.</span></p></body>)/Rect[149.457 372.261 181.567 386.347]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj3261 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 3260 0 R/Rect[595.22 265.932 775.22 385.932]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj3262 0 obj<</Filter/FlateDecode/Length 6606>>stream
