" style="font-size:10.0pt"> The revised wording provides a more precise technical description of the intended requirement.</span></p></body>)/Rect[204.743 289.695 221.054 301.066]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj3466 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 3465 0 R/Rect[595.22 180.731 775.22 300.731]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj3467 0 obj<</AP<</N 9133 0 R>>/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/Contents(\(301\) The term systematic capabilityŽ now replaces safety integrity levelŽ throughout Part 3 \(with a small number of exceptions where the original term is the more appropriate\). This is in recognition of the fact that IEC 61508 can \(in ed2.0\) be a\pplied either to the development of safety related software in a final application system which implements safety functions, or to the development of elements containing software which are intended for use in a safety related system but for which the syst\em design and safety integrity level has not necessarily been determined. Software of systematic capability N \(as created by following the requirements of the Standard\) is capable of being used in a final application system to support a safety function \of SIL N \(or less\), or in some circumstances to support a safety function of SIL N+1 when used in conjunction with other elements.)/CreationDate(D:20100524160339+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20100524172739+02'00')/NM(1bcb5ae6-c2a3-4bdc-859c-07abfd566ca5)/P 3457 0 R/Popup 3468 0 R/QuadPoints[214.567 263.891 234.871 263.891 214.567 253.189 234.871 253.189]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">\(301\)</span><span\ dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt"> The term &#8220;systematic capability&#8221; now replaces &#8220;safety integrity level&#8221; throughout Part 3 \(with a small number of exceptions where the original term is the more appropriate\). This is in recogni\tion of the fact that IEC 61508 can \(in ed2.0\) be applied either to the development of safety related software in a final application system which implements safety functions, or to the development of elements containing software which are intended for \use in a safety related system but for which the system design and safety integrity level has not necessarily been determined. Software of systematic capability N \(as created by following the requirements of the Standard\) is capable of being used in a f\inal application system to support a safety function of SIL N \(or less\), or in some circumstances to support a safety function of SIL N+1 when used in conjunction with other elements.</span></p></body>)/Rect[211.71 252.855 237.728 264.225]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj3468 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 3467 0 R/Rect[595.22 143.891 775.22 263.891]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj3469 0 obj<</AP<</N 9132 0 R>>/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/Contents(\(1\) The term "element" although used extensively in IEC 61508 ed1.0 was not a defined term. The term has now been defined in 3.4.5 of IEC 61508-4 ed2.0.)/CreationDate(D:20100524160547+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20100524172739+02'00')/NM(28d88785-ca23-4a51-b5f4-01a2b2a04064)/P 3457 0 R/Popup 3470 0 R/QuadPoints[339.362 666.851 349.96 666.851 339.362 656.149 349.96 656.149]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">\(1\)</span><span d\ir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt"> The term &quot;element&quot; although used extensively in IEC 61508 ed1.0 was not a defined term. The term has now been defined in 3.4.5 of IEC 61508-4 ed2.0.</span></p></body>)/Rect[336.505 655.815 352.817 667.185]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj3470 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 3469 0 R/Rect[595.22 546.851 775.22 666.851]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj3471 0 obj<</AP<</N 9138 0 R>>/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/Contents(\(346\) Superfluous word\(s\) has \(have\) been deleted.)/CreationDate(D:20100524160718+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20100524172739+02'00')/NM(c580e790-42ba-4b23-85f9-c5a3f5d4714e)/P 3457 0 R/Popup 3472 0 R/QuadPoints[405.482 648.491 425.672 648.491 405.482 637.789 425.672 637.789]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">\(346\) </span><spa\n dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt">Superfluous word\(s\) has \(have\) been deleted.</span></p></body>)/Rect[402.625 637.455 428.529 648.825]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj3472 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 3471 0 R/Rect[595.22 528.491 775.22 648.491]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj3473 0 obj<</AP<</N 9128 0 R>>/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/Contents(\(308\) The new text has been added to correct an important omission from ed1.0.)/CreationDate(D:20100524160805+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20100524172739+02'00')/NM(6a534234-ca2b-4fd3-a493-e7a2b15ce48d)/P 3457 0 R/Popup 3474 0 R/QuadPoints[171.6 150.744 191.79 150.744 171.6 140.042 191.79 140.042]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">\(308\)</span><span\ dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt"> The new text has been added to correct an important omission from ed1.0.</span></p></body>)/Rect[168.743 139.708 194.647 151.078]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj3474 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 3473 0 R/Rect[595.22 30.7437 775.22 150.744]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj3475 0 obj<</Filter/FlateDecode/Length 4429>>stream
