.0pt"> The revised wording provides a more precise technical description of the intended requirement.</span></p></body>)/Rect[433.108 191.661 449.295 203.031]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj3489 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 3488 0 R/Rect[595.22 82.6965 775.22 202.697]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj3490 0 obj<</AP<</N 9155 0 R>>/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/Contents(\(301\) The term systematic capabilityŽ now replaces safety integrity levelŽ throughout Part 3 \(with a small number of exceptions where the original term is the more appropriate\). This is in recognition of the fact that IEC 61508 can \(in ed2.0\) be a\pplied either to the development of safety related software in a final application system which implements safety functions, or to the development of elements containing software which are intended for use in a safety related system but for which the syst\em design and safety integrity level has not necessarily been determined. Software of systematic capability N \(as created by following the requirements of the Standard\) is capable of being used in a final application system to support a safety function \of SIL N \(or less\), or in some circumstances to support a safety function of SIL N+1 when used in conjunction with other elements.)/CreationDate(D:20100524160328+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20100524172739+02'00')/NM(88e63d93-5cb3-462e-a3c1-c71132c5dbf5)/P 3476 0 R/Popup 3491 0 R/QuadPoints[214.567 614.891 234.871 614.891 214.567 604.189 234.871 604.189]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">\(301\)</span><span\ dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt"> The term &#8220;systematic capability&#8221; now replaces &#8220;safety integrity level&#8221; throughout Part 3 \(with a small number of exceptions where the original term is the more appropriate\). This is in recogni\tion of the fact that IEC 61508 can \(in ed2.0\) be applied either to the development of safety related software in a final application system which implements safety functions, or to the development of elements containing software which are intended for \use in a safety related system but for which the system design and safety integrity level has not necessarily been determined. Software of systematic capability N \(as created by following the requirements of the Standard\) is capable of being used in a f\inal application system to support a safety function of SIL N \(or less\), or in some circumstances to support a safety function of SIL N+1 when used in conjunction with other elements.</span></p></body>)/Rect[211.71 603.855 237.728 615.225]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj3491 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 3490 0 R/Rect[595.22 494.891 775.22 614.891]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj3492 0 obj<</AP<</N 9144 0 R>>/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/Contents(\(301\) The term systematic capabilityŽ now replaces safety integrity levelŽ throughout Part 3 \(with a small number of exceptions where the original term is the more appropriate\). This is in recognition of the fact that IEC 61508 can \(in ed2.0\) be a\pplied either to the development of safety related software in a final application system which implements safety functions, or to the development of elements containing software which are intended for use in a safety related system but for which the syst\em design and safety integrity level has not necessarily been determined. Software of systematic capability N \(as created by following the requirements of the Standard\) is capable of being used in a final application system to support a safety function \of SIL N \(or less\), or in some circumstances to support a safety function of SIL N+1 when used in conjunction with other elements.)/CreationDate(D:20100524160358+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20100524172751+02'00')/NM(2595e4da-18d2-47fc-89b1-357ae8f857d4)/P 3476 0 R/Popup 3493 0 R/QuadPoints[255.961 116.291 276.27 116.291 255.961 105.589 276.27 105.589]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">\(301\)</span><span\ dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt"> The term &#8220;systematic capability&#8221; now replaces &#8220;safety integrity level&#8221; throughout Part 3 \(with a small number of exceptions where the original term is the more appropriate\). This is in recogni\tion of the fact that IEC 61508 can \(in ed2.0\) be applied either to the development of safety related software in a final application system which implements safety functions, or to the development of elements containing software which are intended for \use in a safety related system but for which the system design and safety integrity level has not necessarily been determined. Software of systematic capability N \(as created by following the requirements of the Standard\) is capable of being used in a f\inal application system to support a safety function of SIL N \(or less\), or in some circumstances to support a safety function of SIL N+1 when used in conjunction with other elements.</span></p></body>)/Rect[253.104 105.255 279.127 116.625]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj3493 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 3492 0 R/Rect[595.22 -3.70944 775.22 116.291]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj3494 0 obj<</AP<</N 9165 0 R>>/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/Contents(\(1\) The term "element" although used extensively in IEC 61508 ed1.0 was not a defined term. The term has now been defined in 3.4.5 of IEC 61508-4 ed2.0.)/CreationDate(D:20100524160605+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20100524172739+02'00')/NM(92a7d1fa-1c80-4194-ac23-b76a737ba121)/P 3476 0 R/Popup 3495 0 R/QuadPoints[171.597 572.171 182.068 572.171 171.597 561.47 182.068 561.47]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">\(1\)</span><span d\ir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt"> The term &quot;element&quot; although used extensively in IEC 61508 ed1.0 was not a defined term. The term has now been defined in 3.4.5 of IEC 61508-4 ed2.0.</span></p></body>)/Rect[168.74 561.135 184.925 572.506]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj3495 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 3494 0 R/Rect[595.22 452.171 775.22 572.171]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj3496 0 obj<</AP<</N 9164 0 R>>/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/Contents(\(308\) The new text has been added to correct an important omission from ed1.0.)/CreationDate(D:20100524160825+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20100524172751+02'00')/NM(1c3a2414-863b-4247-b1ab-3f2adaa55d58)/P 3476 0 R/Popup 3497 0 R/QuadPoints[171.597 483.385 191.787 483.385 171.597 472.684 191.787 472.684]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">\(308\)</span><span\ dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt"> The new text has been added to correct an important omission from ed1.0.</span></p></body>)/Rect[168.74 472.35 194.644 483.72]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj3497 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 3496 0 R/Rect[595.22 363.385 775.22 483.385]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj3498 0 obj<</Filter/FlateDecode/Length 5145>>stream
