e development of elements containing software which are intended for use in a safety related system but for which the syst\em design and safety integrity level has not necessarily been determined. Software of systematic capability N \(as created by following the requirements of the Standard\) is capable of being used in a final application system to support a safety function \of SIL N \(or less\), or in some circumstances to support a safety function of SIL N+1 when used in conjunction with other elements.)/CreationDate(D:20100524135937+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20100524172751+02'00')/NM(afa210d6-94b3-4ae8-87e9-4f7dd46da809)/P 3499 0 R/Popup 3505 0 R/QuadPoints[493.19 418.34 518.112 418.34 493.19 405.083 518.112 405.083]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">\(301\)</span><span\ dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt"> The term &#8220;systematic capability&#8221; now replaces &#8220;safety integrity level&#8221; throughout Part 3 \(with a small number of exceptions where the original term is the more appropriate\). This is in recogni\tion of the fact that IEC 61508 can \(in ed2.0\) be applied either to the development of safety related software in a final application system which implements safety functions, or to the development of elements containing software which are intended for \use in a safety related system but for which the system design and safety integrity level has not necessarily been determined. Software of systematic capability N \(as created by following the requirements of the Standard\) is capable of being used in a f\inal application system to support a safety function of SIL N \(or less\), or in some circumstances to support a safety function of SIL N+1 when used in conjunction with other elements.</span></p></body>)/Rect[489.651 404.669 521.651 418.754]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj3505 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 3504 0 R/Rect[595.22 298.34 775.22 418.34]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj3506 0 obj<</AP<</N 9176 0 R>>/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/Contents(\(301\) The term systematic capabilityŽ now replaces safety integrity levelŽ throughout Part 3 \(with a small number of exceptions where the original term is the more appropriate\). This is in recognition of the fact that IEC 61508 can \(in ed2.0\) be a\pplied either to the development of safety related software in a final application system which implements safety functions, or to the development of elements containing software which are intended for use in a safety related system but for which the syst\em design and safety integrity level has not necessarily been determined. Software of systematic capability N \(as created by following the requirements of the Standard\) is capable of being used in a final application system to support a safety function \of SIL N \(or less\), or in some circumstances to support a safety function of SIL N+1 when used in conjunction with other elements.)/CreationDate(D:20100524135946+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20100524172751+02'00')/NM(53d58c42-2357-4766-867d-6c5a4d9fcfe2)/P 3499 0 R/Popup 3507 0 R/QuadPoints[346.211 338.78 371.119 338.78 346.211 325.523 371.119 325.523]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">\(301\)</span><span\ dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt"> The term &#8220;systematic capability&#8221; now replaces &#8220;safety integrity level&#8221; throughout Part 3 \(with a small number of exceptions where the original term is the more appropriate\). This is in recogni\tion of the fact that IEC 61508 can \(in ed2.0\) be applied either to the development of safety related software in a final application system which implements safety functions, or to the development of elements containing software which are intended for \use in a safety related system but for which the system design and safety integrity level has not necessarily been determined. Software of systematic capability N \(as created by following the requirements of the Standard\) is capable of being used in a f\inal application system to support a safety function of SIL N \(or less\), or in some circumstances to support a safety function of SIL N+1 when used in conjunction with other elements.</span></p></body>)/Rect[342.672 325.109 374.658 339.194]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj3507 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 3506 0 R/Rect[595.22 218.78 775.22 338.78]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj3508 0 obj<</AP<</N 9180 0 R>>/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/Contents(\(4\) The revised wording provides a more precise technical description of the intended requirement.)/CreationDate(D:20100524155527+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20100524172751+02'00')/NM(a7e5bc3f-81c1-4ccb-b071-286361c03bfd)/P 3499 0 R/Popup 3509 0 R/QuadPoints[229.56 577.341 240.152 577.341 229.56 566.639 240.152 566.639]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">\(4\)</span><span d\ir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt"> The revised wording provides a more precise technical description of the intended requirement.</span></p></body>)/Rect[226.704 566.305 243.009 577.675]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj3509 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 3508 0 R/Rect[595.22 457.341 775.22 577.341]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj3510 0 obj<</AP<</N 9178 0 R>>/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/Contents(\(346\) Superfluous word\(s\) has \(have\) been deleted.)/CreationDate(D:20100524160743+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20100524172751+02'00')/NM(95629e13-db91-4381-bafb-90063ba2c4cf)/P 3499 0 R/Popup 3511 0 R/QuadPoints[255.841 676.089 