tem but for which the syst\em design and safety integrity level has not necessarily been determined. Software of systematic capability N \(as created by following the requirements of the Standard\) is capable of being used in a final application system to support a safety function \of SIL N \(or less\), or in some circumstances to support a safety function of SIL N+1 when used in conjunction with other elements.)/CreationDate(D:20100524140002+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20100524172801+02'00')/NM(72d2ced9-6738-4588-ac8e-25c660aa1527)/P 3593 0 R/Popup 3600 0 R/QuadPoints[429.243 757.7 454.154 757.7 429.243 744.443 454.154 744.443]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">\(301\)</span><span\ dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt"> The term &#8220;systematic capability&#8221; now replaces &#8220;safety integrity level&#8221; throughout Part 3 \(with a small number of exceptions where the original term is the more appropriate\). This is in recogni\tion of the fact that IEC 61508 can \(in ed2.0\) be applied either to the development of safety related software in a final application system which implements safety functions, or to the development of elements containing software which are intended for \use in a safety related system but for which the system design and safety integrity level has not necessarily been determined. Software of systematic capability N \(as created by following the requirements of the Standard\) is capable of being used in a f\inal application system to support a safety function of SIL N \(or less\), or in some circumstances to support a safety function of SIL N+1 when used in conjunction with other elements.</span></p></body>)/Rect[425.703 744.029 457.693 758.114]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj3600 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 3599 0 R/Rect[595.22 637.7 775.22 757.7]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj3601 0 obj<</AP<</N 9246 0 R>>/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/Contents(\(307\) The new text regarding independence has been introduced because ed2.0 allows SIL N functions to be achieved by a combination of system elements of SIL N-1 \(systematic capability N-1\).)/CreationDate(D:20100524140354+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20100524172801+02'00')/NM(6544a203-0d9a-4f84-9701-f466f2c05228)/P 3593 0 R/Popup 3602 0 R/QuadPoints[332.518 705.38 357.306 705.38 332.518 692.123 357.306 692.123]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">\(307\)</span><span\ dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt"> The new text regarding independence has been introduced because ed2.0 allows SIL N functions to be achieved by a combination of system elements of SIL N-1 \(systematic capability N-1\).</span></p></body>)/Rect[328.979 691.709 360.845 705.794]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj3602 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 3601 0 R/Rect[595.22 585.38 775.22 705.38]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj3603 0 obj<</AP<</N 9247 0 R>>/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/Contents(\(311\) Subclauses 7.2.2.11, 7.2.2.12 and 7.2.2.13 have been moved into 7.2 \(from 7.3 in ed1.0\).)/CreationDate(D:20100524140811+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20100524172801+02'00')/NM(bceafb4e-a2c0-4423-b9a4-d9afd263338a)/P 3593 0 R/Popup 3604 0 R/QuadPoints[120.121 683.896 145.029 683.896 120.121 670.64 145.029 670.64]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">\(311\) </span><spa\n dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt">Subclauses</span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold"> </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt">7.2.2.11, 7.2.2.12 and 7.2.2.13 have been moved into 7.2 \(from 7.3 in ed1.0\).</span></p></bo\dy>)/Rect[116.582 670.225 148.568 684.311]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj3604 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 3603 0 R/Rect[595.22 563.896 775.22 683.896]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj3605 0 obj<</Filter/FlateDecode/Length 5257>>stream
