 of exceptions where the original term is the more appropriate\). This is in recognition of the fact that IEC 61508 can \(in ed2.0\) be a\pplied either to the development of safety related software in a final application system which implements safety functions, or to the development of elements containing software which are intended for use in a safety related system but for which the syst\em design and safety integrity level has not necessarily been determined. Software of systematic capability N \(as created by following the requirements of the Standard\) is capable of being used in a final application system to support a safety function \of SIL N \(or less\), or in some circumstances to support a safety function of SIL N+1 when used in conjunction with other elements.)/CreationDate(D:20100524140009+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20100524172801+02'00')/NM(8290d36e-df6a-450e-ae47-e5d3708f5f27)/P 3610 0 R/Popup 3620 0 R/QuadPoints[238.32 378.26 263.232 378.26 238.32 365.0 263.232 365.003]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">\(301\)</span><span\ dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt"> The term &#8220;systematic capability&#8221; now replaces &#8220;safety integrity level&#8221; throughout Part 3 \(with a small number of exceptions where the original term is the more appropriate\). This is in recogni\tion of the fact that IEC 61508 can \(in ed2.0\) be applied either to the development of safety related software in a final application system which implements safety functions, or to the development of elements containing software which are intended for \use in a safety related system but for which the system design and safety integrity level has not necessarily been determined. Software of systematic capability N \(as created by following the requirements of the Standard\) is capable of being used in a f\inal application system to support a safety function of SIL N \(or less\), or in some circumstances to support a safety function of SIL N+1 when used in conjunction with other elements.</span></p></body>)/Rect[234.781 364.585 266.771 378.674]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj3620 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 3619 0 R/Rect[595.22 258.26 775.22 378.26]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj3621 0 obj<</AP<</N 9273 0 R>>/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/Contents(\(308\) The new text has been added to correct an important omission from ed1.0.)/CreationDate(D:20100524140432+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20100524172801+02'00')/NM(7f45d10e-46f3-4014-b93d-5d165869f167)/P 3610 0 R/Popup 3622 0 R/QuadPoints[142.073 485.262 166.995 485.262 142.073 472.005 166.995 472.005]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">\(308\)</span><span\ dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt"> The new text has been added to correct an important omission from ed1.0.</span></p></body>)/Rect[138.534 471.591 170.534 485.677]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj3622 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 3621 0 R/Rect[595.22 365.262 775.22 485.262]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj3623 0 obj<</AP<</N 9270 0 R>>/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/Contents(\(312\) This subclause has been deleted since it is covered by other requirements.)/CreationDate(D:20100524140837+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20100524172801+02'00')/NM(3a30a759-5491-4172-aff5-740c7409f1a5)/P 3610 0 R/Popup 3624 0 R/QuadPoints[459.36 361.7 484.272 361.7 459.36 348.443 484.272 348.443]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">\(312\) </span><spa\n dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt">This subclause has been deleted since it is covered by other requirements.</span></p></body>)/Rect[455.821 348.029 487.811 362.114]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj3624 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 3623 0 R/Rect[595.22 241.7 775.22 361.7]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj3625 0 obj<</AP<</N 9262 0 R>>/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/Contents(\(313\) This text has been added in recognition of the fact that not all testing will require calibrated tools and equipment.)/CreationDate(D:20100524140904+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20100524172801+02'00')/NM(afb579c6-fb98-4c21-a260-496e6f3e6313)/P 3610 0 R/Popup 3626 0 R/QuadPoints[258.725 333.74 283.627 333.74 258.725 320.483 283.627 320.483]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">\(313\) </span><spa\n dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt">This text has been added in recognition of the fact that not all testing will require calibrated tools and equipment.</span></p></body>)/Rect[255.186 320.069 287.166 334.154]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj3626 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 3625 0 R/Rect[595.22 213.74 775.22 333.74]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj3627 0 obj<</AP<</N 9265 0 R>>/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/Contents(\(314\) This clause has been introduced to emphasise the need to explain the validation strategy, which will for example assist with functional safety assessment.)/CreationDate(D:20100524140944+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20100524172801+02'00')/NM(c62c90b6-4a3c-43fc-be4a-3a11cb311cd5)/P 3610 0 R/Popup 3628 0 R/QuadPoints[423.836 248.66 448.755 248.66 423.836 235.403 448.755 235.403]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">\(314\) </span><spa\n dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt">This clause has been introduced to emphasise the need to explain the validation strategy, which will for example assist with functional safety assessment.</span></p></body>)/Rect[420.297 234.989 452.294 249.074]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj3628 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 3627 0 R/Rect[595.22 128.66 775.22 248.66]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj3629 0 obj<</AP<</N 9276 0 R>>/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/Contents(\(315\) This clause has been added to provide a link with the idea of rigour of evidence as introduced in the properties Tables in Annex C. Objective measures of, for example, structural or requirements coverage can offer more rigorous evidence than exper\t judgement, although the latter is sometimes the only form of evidence available.)/CreationDate(D:20100524140951+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20100524172801+02'00')/NM(53683c9a-c162-4c4f-b5e1-fbe12cffd636)/P 3610 0 R/Popup 3630 0 R/QuadPoints[491.042 154.561 515.95 154.561 491.042 141.305 515.95 141.305]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">\(315\) </span><spa\n dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt">This clause has been added to provide a link with the idea of rigour of evidence as introduced in the properties Tables in Annex C. Objective measures of, for example, structural or requirements coverage can offer more\ rigorous evidence than expert judgement, although the latter is sometimes the only form of evidence available.</span></p></body>)/Rect[487.503 140.89 519.489 154.976]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj3630 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 3629 0 R/Rect[595.22 34.5612 775.22 154.561]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj3631 0 obj<</Filter/FlateDecode/Length 5478>>stream
