ed requirement.)/CreationDate(D:20100523162548+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20100524172801+02'00')/NM(aa7c431b-e77f-463b-afc2-a5f63ad165e1)/P 3633 0 R/Popup 3640 0 R/QuadPoints[463.682 426.5 476.6 426.5 463.682 413.243 476.6 413.243]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">\(4\)</span><span d\ir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt"> The revised wording provides a more precise technical description of the intended requirement.</span></p></body>)/Rect[460.142 412.829 480.139 426.914]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj3640 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 3639 0 R/Rect[595.22 306.5 775.22 426.5]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj3641 0 obj<</AP<</N 9288 0 R>>/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/Contents(\(301\) The term systematic capabilityŽ now replaces safety integrity levelŽ throughout Part 3 \(with a small number of exceptions where the original term is the more appropriate\). This is in recognition of the fact that IEC 61508 can \(in ed2.0\) be a\pplied either to the development of safety related software in a final application system which implements safety functions, or to the development of elements containing software which are intended for use in a safety related system but for which the syst\em design and safety integrity level has not necessarily been determined. Software of systematic capability N \(as created by following the requirements of the Standard\) is capable of being used in a final application system to support a safety function \of SIL N \(or less\), or in some circumstances to support a safety function of SIL N+1 when used in conjunction with other elements.)/CreationDate(D:20100524140017+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20100524172801+02'00')/NM(d2bbe80a-e101-4174-a911-92807cf43ec4)/P 3633 0 R/Popup 3642 0 R/QuadPoints[331.677 353.9 356.584 353.9 331.677 340.643 356.584 340.643]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">\(301\)</span><span\ dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt"> The term &#8220;systematic capability&#8221; now replaces &#8220;safety integrity level&#8221; throughout Part 3 \(with a small number of exceptions where the original term is the more appropriate\). This is in recogni\tion of the fact that IEC 61508 can \(in ed2.0\) be applied either to the development of safety related software in a final application system which implements safety functions, or to the development of elements containing software which are intended for \use in a safety related system but for which the system design and safety integrity level has not necessarily been determined. Software of systematic capability N \(as created by following the requirements of the Standard\) is capable of being used in a f\inal application system to support a safety function of SIL N \(or less\), or in some circumstances to support a safety function of SIL N+1 when used in conjunction with other elements.</span></p></body>)/Rect[328.138 340.229 360.123 354.314]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj3642 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 3641 0 R/Rect[595.22 233.9 775.22 353.9]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj3643 0 obj<</AP<</N 9284 0 R>>/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/Contents(\(308\) The new text has been added to correct an important omission from ed1.0.)/CreationDate(D:20100524140440+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20100524172801+02'00')/NM(49e575d1-a964-4364-8bf8-9903931a006f)/P 3633 0 R/Popup 3644 0 R/QuadPoints[202.206 476.037 225.436 476.037 202.206 462.781 225.436 462.781]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">\(308\)</span><span\ dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt"> The new text has been added to correct an important omission from ed1.0.</span></p></body>)/Rect[198.667 462.366 228.975 476.452]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj3644 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 3643 0 R/Rect[595.22 356.037 775.22 476.037]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj3645 0 obj<</AP<</N 9289 0 R>>/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/Contents(\(316\) The new text has been introduced to recognise the importance of systems configured by application data and the need to treat such data with the same degree of rigour as safety related software.)/CreationDate(D:20100524141046+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20100524172811+02'00')/NM(3cf8eb0a-5c7b-44ca-a9c4-9c79029d811d)/P 3633 0 R/Popup 3646 0 R/QuadPoints[236.515 304.449 261.422 304.449 236.515 291.192 261.422 291.192]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">\(316\) </span><spa\n dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt">The new text has been introduced to recognise the importance of systems configured by application data and the need to treat such data with the same degree of rigour as safety related software.</span></p></body>)/Rect[232.976 290.777 264.961 304.863]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj3646 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 3645 0 R/Rect[595.22 184.449 775.22 304.449]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj3647 0 obj<</AP<</N 9296 0 R>>/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/Contents(\(317\) This text has been added to clarify the meaning of supplierŽ and userŽ, which were somewhat unclear in ed1.0.)/CreationDate(D:20100524141133+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20100524172811+02'00')/NM(323a00fc-6af6-4c52-bc63-1d06f537d00a)/P 3633 0 R/Popup 3648 0 R/QuadPoints[118.558 228.593 143.361 228.593 118.558 215.337 143.361 215.337]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://w