9.18]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj3694 0 obj<</AP<</N 9328 0 R>>/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/Contents(\(323\) In ed2.0, there are three ways to demonstrate that software will have a given systematic capability; these are known as routes 1, 2 and 3 with subscripts sŽ in line with the system and hardware routes given in 61508-2 ed2.0. Two of the routes are\ the same as those in ed1.0 … development of \(new\) software in accordance with the requirements of the Standard, and proven in use \(the term routeŽ did not exist in ed1.0\). The third route 3s is new and allows for the re-use of software which does no\t meet the very stringent proven in useŽ requirements. This is one of the most significant changes in ed2.0.)/CreationDate(D:20100524141408+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20100524172811+02'00')/NM(8374d42e-a4f6-4d2d-b4d0-737219b30e5c)/P 3679 0 R/Popup 3695 0 R/QuadPoints[112.563 303.974 137.602 303.974 112.563 290.717 137.602 290.717]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">\(323\) </span><spa\n dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt">In ed2.0, there are three ways to demonstrate that software will have a given systematic capability; these are known as routes 1, 2 and 3 with subscripts &#8220;s&#8221; in line with the system and hardware routes give\n in 61508-2 ed2.0. Two of the routes are the same as those in ed1.0 &#8211; development of \(new\) software in accordance with the requirements of the Standard, and proven in use \(the term &#8220;route&#8221; did not exist in ed1.0\). The third route 3<\/span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;vertical-align:-5.0pt">s</span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt"> is new and allows for the re-use of software which does not meet the very stringent &#8220;proven in use&#8221; requirements. This is on\e of the most significant changes in ed2.0.</span></p></body>)/Rect[109.024 290.302 141.141 304.388]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj3695 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 3694 0 R/Rect[595.22 183.974 775.22 303.974]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj3696 0 obj<</AP<</N 9333 0 R>>/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/Contents(\(324\) The requirement for a safety manual has been introduced to support the use of pre-existing elements in safety related applications. The safety manual contains all the information which a developer of a final application system needs in order to ju\dge whether a pre-existing element is suitable for that application, and to provide the necessary supporting safety evidence. A supplier of products intended for use in safety related applications is expected to provide the safety manual to accompany the \product.)/CreationDate(D:20100524141424+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20100524172819+02'00')/NM(36c2ed7b-29bf-42dd-8eea-2d2d64683d6d)/P 3679 0 R/Popup 3697 0 R/QuadPoints[252.481 72.7289 277.52 72.7289 252.481 59.4722 277.52 59.4722]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">\(324\) </span><spa\n dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt">The requirement for a safety manual has been introduced to support the use of pre-existing elements in safety related applications. The safety manual contains all the information which a developer of a final applicatio\n system needs in order to judge whether a pre-existing element is suitable for that application, and to provide the necessary supporting safety evidence. A supplier of products intended for use in safety related applications is expected to provide the sa\fety manual to accompany the product.</span></p></body>)/Rect[248.942 59.0577 281.059 73.1433]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj3697 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 3696 0 R/Rect[595.22 -47.2711 775.22 72.7289]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj3698 0 obj<</Filter/FlateDecode/Length 7363>>stream
