mlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">\(301\)</span><span\ dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt"> The term &#8220;systematic capability&#8221; now replaces &#8220;safety integrity level&#8221; throughout Part 3 \(with a small number of exceptions where the original term is the more appropriate\). This is in recogni\tion of the fact that IEC 61508 can \(in ed2.0\) be applied either to the development of safety related software in a final application system which implements safety functions, or to the development of elements containing software which are intended for \use in a safety related system but for which the system design and safety integrity level has not necessarily been determined. Software of systematic capability N \(as created by following the requirements of the Standard\) is capable of being used in a f\inal application system to support a safety function of SIL N \(or less\), or in some circumstances to support a safety function of SIL N+1 when used in conjunction with other elements.</span></p></body>)/Rect[270.298 318.629 302.28 332.714]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj4078 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 4077 0 R/Rect[595.22 212.3 775.22 332.3]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj4079 0 obj<</AP<</N 9536 0 R>>/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/Contents(\(326\) These \(informative\) Tables of software properties have been added to explain or clarify the purpose of the various techniques and measures listed in Annexes A and B. In ed1.0, the techniques were recommendedŽ or highly recommendedŽ without any\ description of, or guidance on, what the use of each technique was seeking to achieve. The Tables of properties can also be used by software developers to select and justify the use of techniques and measures which are not listed in the Annexes A and B T\ables but which nevertheless can be shown to contribute to the achievement of one or more software properties.)/CreationDate(D:20100524141947+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20100524172848+02'00')/NM(cd7bcada-fc15-440b-bff5-576e6e8bbe43)/P 4055 0 R/Popup 4080 0 R/QuadPoints[262.441 154.701 282.755 154.701 262.441 144.0 282.755 144.0]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">\(326\) </span><spa\n dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt">These \(informative\) Tables of software properties have been added to explain or clarify the purpose of the various techniques and measures listed in Annexes A and B. In ed1.0, the techniques were &#8220;recommended&#\8221; or &#8220;highly recommended&#8221; without any description of, or guidance on, what the use of each technique was seeking to achieve. The Tables of properties can also be used by software developers to select and justify the use of techniques and m\easures which are not listed in the Annexes A and B Tables but which nevertheless can be shown to contribute to the achievement of one or more software properties.</span></p></body>)/Rect[259.584 143.666 285.611 155.036]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj4080 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 4079 0 R/Rect[595.22 34.7013 775.22 154.701]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj4081 0 obj<</AP<</N 9530 0 R>>/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/Contents(\(352\) Subclause 7.7.2.7 in ed1.0 which covered tool qualification has been replaced by this reference to 7.4.4 which provides much more detailed requirements.)/CreationDate(D:20100524143748+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20100524172848+02'00')/NM(026e0c15-023a-4fca-9e26-c11076eaba56)/P 4055 0 R/Popup 4082 0 R/QuadPoints[363.475 626.42 388.383 626.42 363.475 613.163 388.383 613.163]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">\(352\) </span><spa\n dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt">Subclause 7.7.2.7 in ed1.0 which covered tool qualification has been replaced by this reference to 7.4.4 which provides much more detailed requirements.</span></p></body>)/Rect[359.936 612.749 391.922 626.834]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj4082 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 4081 0 R/Rect[595.22 506.42 775.22 626.42]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj4083 0 obj<</Filter/FlateDecode/Length 5660>>stream
