="font-size:10.0pt"> The revised wording provides a more precise technical description of the intended requirement.</span></p></body>)/Rect[323.456 106.09 343.45 120.176]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj4317 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 4316 0 R/Rect[595.22 -0.238571 775.22 119.761]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj4318 0 obj<</AP<</N 9695 0 R>>/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/Contents(\(301\) The term systematic capabilityŽ now replaces safety integrity levelŽ throughout Part 3 \(with a small number of exceptions where the original term is the more appropriate\). This is in recognition of the fact that IEC 61508 can \(in ed2.0\) be a\pplied either to the development of safety related software in a final application system which implements safety functions, or to the development of elements containing software which are intended for use in a safety related system but for which the syst\em design and safety integrity level has not necessarily been determined. Software of systematic capability N \(as created by following the requirements of the Standard\) is capable of being used in a final application system to support a safety function \of SIL N \(or less\), or in some circumstances to support a safety function of SIL N+1 when used in conjunction with other elements.)/CreationDate(D:20100524140039+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20100524172917+02'00')/NM(c3741052-10a5-4bda-9334-e2810196fd27)/P 4312 0 R/Popup 4319 0 R/QuadPoints[70.9237 230.296 95.714 230.296 70.9237 217.039 95.714 217.039]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">\(301\)</span><span\ dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt"> The term &#8220;systematic capability&#8221; now replaces &#8220;safety integrity level&#8221; throughout Part 3 \(with a small number of exceptions where the original term is the more appropriate\). This is in recogni\tion of the fact that IEC 61508 can \(in ed2.0\) be applied either to the development of safety related software in a final application system which implements safety functions, or to the development of elements containing software which are intended for \use in a safety related system but for which the system design and safety integrity level has not necessarily been determined. Software of systematic capability N \(as created by following the requirements of the Standard\) is capable of being used in a f\inal application system to support a safety function of SIL N \(or less\), or in some circumstances to support a safety function of SIL N+1 when used in conjunction with other elements.</span></p></body>)/Rect[67.3847 216.625 99.2531 230.71]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj4319 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 4318 0 R/Rect[595.22 110.296 775.22 230.296]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj4320 0 obj<</AP<</N 9699 0 R>>/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/Contents(\(326\) These \(informative\) Tables of software properties have been added to explain or clarify the purpose of the various techniques and measures listed in Annexes A and B. In ed1.0, the techniques were recommendedŽ or highly recommendedŽ without any\ description of, or guidance on, what the use of each technique was seeking to achieve. The Tables of properties can also be used by software developers to select and justify the use of techniques and measures which are not listed in the Annexes A and B T\ables but which nevertheless can be shown to contribute to the achievement of one or more software properties.)/CreationDate(D:20100524142015+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20100524172917+02'00')/NM(beae8671-e6f0-44bb-91aa-038a29713186)/P 4312 0 R/Popup 4321 0 R/QuadPoints[422.88 195.617 447.787 195.617 422.88 182.36 447.787 182.36]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">\(326\) </span><spa\n dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt">These \(informative\) Tables of software properties have been added to explain or clarify the purpose of the various techniques and measures listed in Annexes A and B. In ed1.0, the techniques were &#8220;recommended&#\8221; or &#8220;highly recommended&#8221; without any description of, or guidance on, what the use of each technique was seeking to achieve. The Tables of properties can also be used by software developers to select and justify the use of techniques and m\easures which are not listed in the Annexes A and B Tables but which nevertheless can be shown to contribute to the achievement of one or more software properties.</span></p></body>)/Rect[419.341 181.946 451.327 196.031]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj4321 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 4320 0 R/Rect[595.22 75.6168 775.22 195.617]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj4322 0 obj<</AP<</N 9703 0 R>>/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/Contents(\(356\) The description of the examples has been made more precise.)/CreationDate(D:20100524143947+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20100524172917+02'00')/NM(a794bc9c-065d-435d-8849-9654f2347351)/P 4312 0 R/Popup 4323 0 R/QuadPoints[216.962 108.14 241.864 108.14 216.962 94.8833 241.864 94.8833]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">\(356\) </span><spa\n dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt">The description of the examples has been made more precise.</span></p></body>)/Rect[213.423 94.4689 245.403 108.554]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj4323 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 4322 0 R/Rect[595.22 -11.86 775.22 108.14]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj4324 0 obj<</AP<</N 9704 0 R>>/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/Contents(\(354\) This change has been introduced to emphasise the fact that alternative techniques to those listed in Annexes A and B can be used provided that the requirements of the Standard are met. The Tables of properties in Annex C can be used to justify the\ use of particular techniques, where the technique can be shown to help the achievement of the desired properties.)/CreationDate(D:20100524144912+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20100524172917+02'00')/NM(b9dbdc85-a4f3-452e-b978-35f70323615e)/P 4312 0 R/Popup 4325 0 R/QuadPoints[446.641 340.562 471.561 340.562 446.641 327.305 471.561 327.305]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">\(354\) </span><spa\n dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt">This change has been introduced to emphasise the fact that alternative techniques to those listed in Annexes A and B can be used provided that the requirements of the Standard are met. The Tables of properties in Annex\ C can be used to justify the use of particular techniques, where the technique can be shown to help the achievement of the desired properties.</span></p></body>)/Rect[443.102 326.891 475.1 340.976]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj4325 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 4324 0 R/Rect[595.22 220.562 775.22 340.562]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj4326 0 obj<</Filter/FlateDecode/Length 5061>>stream
