-weight:bold">\(416\)</span><span\ dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt"> </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">logic system: </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt">This definition has been removed since the term is no longer used in IEC 61508 ed2.0 and wh\ere previously used has been replaced by a generic term rather than &#8220;logic system&#8221; which is not a common term in all sectors.</span></p></body>)/Rect[135.058 259.589 166.805 273.675]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj4995 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 4994 0 R/Rect[595.22 153.26 775.22 273.26]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj4996 0 obj<</AP<</N 10045 0 R>>/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/Contents(\(417\) subsystem: This is a new definition. The term subsystem was not a defined term in IEC 61508 ed1.0. The use of the term subsystem, as now defined, will mean that it will only be correct to use the term "subsystem" when knowledge of the application \is known since it will be necessary to have knowledge of the dangerous failures associated with the specified safety function.)/CreationDate(D:20100524163103+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20100524173035+02'00')/NM(0d9ad343-637c-48dc-99c6-b726e85daa3a)/P 4986 0 R/Popup 4997 0 R/QuadPoints[129.236 136.458 153.904 136.458 129.236 123.201 153.904 123.201]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">\(417\)</span><span\ dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt"> </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">subsystem: </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt">This is a new definition</span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">.</sp\an><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt"> The term subsystem was not a defined term in IEC 61508 ed1.0. The use of the term subsystem, as now defined, will mean that it will only be correct to use the term &quot;subsystem&quot; when knowledge of the ap\plication is known since it will be necessary to have knowledge of the dangerous failures associated with the specified safety function.</span></p></body>)/Rect[125.697 122.787 157.443 136.872]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj4997 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 4996 0 R/Rect[595.22 16.4577 775.22 136.458]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj4998 0 obj<</Filter/FlateDecode/Length 4095>>stream
