/N 10120 0 R>>/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/Contents(\(440\) Safe Failure Fraction \(SFF\): This is a new definition. The description for safe failure fraction used in IEC 61508 ed1.0 may appear to be similar to the new definition but the focus in IEC 61508 ed1.0 was the application to a subsystem; see 3.4.\4 of IEC 61508-4 ed2.0;  whereas in IEC 61508 ed2.0 the focus is on an element; see 3.4.5 of IEC 61508-4 ed2.0.)/CreationDate(D:20100524164413+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20100524173054+02'00')/NM(6371b4fb-b4a9-4a4d-93ef-b099ddee8db8)/P 5087 0 R/Popup 5094 0 R/QuadPoints[173.518 204.738 198.187 204.738 173.518 191.481 198.187 191.481]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">\(440\) Safe Failur\e Fraction \(SFF\): </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt">This is a new definition. The description for safe failure fraction used in IEC 61508 ed1.0 may appear to be similar to the new definition but the focus in IEC 61508 ed1.0 was the applica\tion to a subsystem; see 3.4.4 of IEC 61508-4 ed2.0;  whereas in IEC 61508 ed2.0 the focus is on an element; see 3.4.5 of IEC 61508-4 ed2.0.</span></p></body>)/Rect[169.979 191.067 201.726 205.152]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj5094 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 5093 0 R/Rect[595.22 84.7377 775.22 204.738]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj5095 0 obj<</Filter/FlateDecode/Length 3264>>stream
