re fully explain how the concept of fail safeŽ fits within the framework of IEC 61508. The modified wording is set out in the last bullet of the Introduction.)/CreationDate(D:20100523164919+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20100524173129+02'00')/NM(ea54f8ab-5efe-4bf3-b74d-7bc9fe5c6c83)/P 5754 0 R/Popup 5767 0 R/QuadPoints[133.2 362.3 146.118 362.3 133.2 349.043 146.118 349.043]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">\(5\) </span><span \dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt">The revised wording has been introduced for this bullet to more fully explain how the concept of &#8220;fail safe&#8221; fits within the framework of IEC 61508. The modified wording is set out in the last bullet of the I\ntroduction.</span></p></body>)/Rect[129.661 348.629 149.657 362.714]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj5767 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 5766 0 R/Rect[595.22 242.3 775.22 362.3]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj5768 0 obj<</AP<</N 10301 0 R>>/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/Contents(\(6\) The purpose of this Note is to indicate that although IEC 61508 sets lower limits on what can be claimed for the target failure measures, which are specified in the clause associated with the Note, it may be possible to achieve even smaller target f\ailure measures \(i.e. more onerous\) than are specified in IEC 61508 for non-complex systems.)/CreationDate(D:20100523165112+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20100524173129+02'00')/NM(40ed1728-3bd9-424c-a23f-36f91ee85658)/P 5754 0 R/Popup 5769 0 R/QuadPoints[463.803 547.573 474.279 547.573 463.803 536.872 474.279 536.872]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">\(6\) </span><span \dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt">The purpose of this Note is to indicate that although IEC 61508 sets lower limits on what can be claimed for the target failure measures, which are specified in the clause associated with the Note, it may be possible to \achieve even smaller target failure measures \(i.e. more onerous\) than are specified in IEC 61508 for non-complex systems.</span></p></body>)/Rect[460.946 536.537 477.135 547.908]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj5769 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 5768 0 R/Rect[595.22 427.573 775.22 547.573]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj5770 0 obj<</AP<</N 10300 0 R>>/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/Contents(\(7\) The revised wording in this bullet sets out explicitly what numerical targets can be claimed in respect of a specified safety function if all relevant requirements in IEC 61508 are met. The concept was not stated explicitly in ed1.0 but this stateme\nt does not represent any change to the way IEC 61508 ed2.0 is intended to be applied compared to IEC 61508 ed1.0.)/CreationDate(D:20100523165251+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20100524173129+02'00')/NM(263ad445-8536-431d-9ac3-26547d69b247)/P 5754 0 R/Popup 5771 0 R/QuadPoints[392.16 475.801 405.197 475.801 392.16 462.544 405.197 462.544]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">\(7\) </span><span \dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt">The revised wording in this bullet sets out explicitly what numerical targets can be claimed in respect of a specified safety function if all relevant requirements in IEC 61508 are met. The concept was not stated explici\tly in ed1.0 but this statement does not represent any change to the way IEC 61508 ed2.0 is intended to be applied compared to IEC 61508 ed1.0.</span></p></body>)/Rect[388.621 462.13 408.736 476.215]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj5771 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 5770 0 R/Rect[595.22 355.801 775.22 475.801]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj5772 0 obj<</AP<</N 10304 0 R>>/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/Contents(\(8\) This is a new concept to IEC 61508 ed2.0; see 7.4.3 of IEC 61508-2 and 3.5.9 of IEC 61508-4\).)/CreationDate(D:20100523165449+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20100524173129+02'00')/NM(f5e590a7-ddec-4171-a8d1-56e83c70df08)/P 5754 0 R/Popup 5773 0 R/QuadPoints[187.681 436.31 200.719 436.31 187.681 423.053 200.719 423.053]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">\(8\) </span><span \dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt">This is a new concept to IEC 61508 ed2.0; see 7.4.3 of IEC 61508-2 and 3.5.9 of IEC 61508-4\).</span></p></body>)/Rect[184.142 422.638 204.258 436.724]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj5773 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 5772 0 R/Rect[595.22 316.31 775.22 436.31]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj5774 0 obj<</AP<</N 10303 0 R>>/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/Contents(\(9\) New wording has been introduced to IEC 61508 ed2.0 for this bullet to more fully explain how the concept of fail safeŽ fits within the framework of IEC 61508; see Explanation 5.)/CreationDate(D:20100523165609+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20100524173129+02'00')/NM(80a66ca6-bb7e-4d2e-b1ec-f917d98df12f)/P 5754 0 R/Popup 5775 0 R/QuadPoints[284.871 339.372 297.908 339.372 284.871 326.115 297.908 326.115]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">\(9\) </span><span \dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt">New wording has been introduced to IEC 61508 ed2.0 for this bullet to more fully explain how the concept of &#8220;fail safe&#8221; fits within the framework of IEC 61508; see Explanati