 a percentage of undetected failure in the comparison between the two channel architecture.)/CreationDate(D:20100523180638+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20100524173151+02'00')/NM(83de305b-615d-43fd-9d19-85742c399b0d)/P 6068 0 R/Popup 6073 0 R/QuadPoints[477.843 757.946 505.149 757.946 477.843 743.252 505.149 743.252]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">\(600\)</span><span\ dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt"> The changes in Tables B.1 to B.13 have arisen because in IEC 61508-6 ed1.0 the failure rate figures used in the Tables were the </span><span dir="ltr" style="text-decoration:underline;font-size:10.0pt">total</span><spa\n dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt"> failure rate of the elements with the assumption that the split between safe and dangerous was 50 % safe and 50 % dangerous. However, for IEC 61508-6 ed2.0 it was considered that it would be clearer to just use the da\ngerous failure rate for each element. Therefore, the split between dangerous failure and safe failure is no longer relevant. &#13;Also the formula for the 1oo2D was updated to include a percentage of undetected failure in the comparison between the two c\hannel architecture.</span></p></body>)/Rect[473.921 742.793 509.072 758.406]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj6073 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 6072 0 R/Rect[595.22 637.946 775.22 757.946]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj6074 0 obj<</AP<</N 10384 0 R>>/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/Contents(\(100\) For the definition of MTTRŽ and MRTŽ, see 3.6.21 and 3.6.22 of IEC 61508-4 ed2.0 respectively.)/CreationDate(D:20100523183451+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20100524173151+02'00')/NM(74da1865-3b5c-4a36-9231-e36b61fdecba)/P 6068 0 R/Popup 6075 0 R/QuadPoints[153.47 297.885 178.395 297.885 153.47 284.595 178.395 284.595]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/