endstreamendobj6104 0 obj<</Annots 6105 0 R/Contents 6108 0 R/CropBox[0 0 595.22 842]/MediaBox[0 0 595.22 842]/Parent 11463 0 R/Resources<</ExtGState<</GS0 7162 0 R>>/Font<</C2_0 10380 0 R/C2_1 10373 0 R/T1_0 10283 0 R/TT0 10280 0 R/TT1 10285 0 R/TT2 10284 0 R/TT3 10312 0 R>>/ProcSet[/PDF/Text]>>/Rotate 0/Thumb 11063 0 R/Type/Page>>endobj6105 0 obj[6106 0 R 6107 0 R]endobj6106 0 obj<</AP<</N 10402 0 R>>/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/Contents(\(600\) The changes in Tables B.1 to B.13 have arisen because in IEC 61508-6 ed1.0 the failure rate figures used in the Tables were the total failure rate of the elements with the assumption that the split between safe and dangerous was 50 % safe and 50 %\ dangerous. However, for IEC 61508-6 ed2.0 it was considered that it would be clearer to just use the dangerous failure rate for each element. Therefore, the split between dangerous failure and safe failure is no longer relevant. \rAlso the formula for th\e 1oo2D was updated to include a percentage of undetected failure in the comparison between the two channel architecture.)/CreationDate(D:20100523180700+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20100524173151+02'00')/NM(b98de8ac-532c-4e51-a11a-296348965a1f)/P 6104 0 R/Popup 6107 0 R/QuadPoints[122.162 663.891 147.082 663.891 122.162 650.593 147.082 650.593]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">\(600\)</span><span\ dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt"> The changes in Tables B.1 to B.13 have arisen because in IEC 61508-6 ed1.0 the failure rate figures used in the Tables were the </span><span dir="ltr" style="text-decoration:underline;font-size:10.0pt">total</span><spa\n dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt"> failure rate of the elements with the assumption that the split between safe and dangerous was 50 % safe and 50 % dangerous. However, for IEC 61508-6 ed2.0 it was considered that it would be clearer to just use the da\ngerous failure rate for each element. Therefore, the split between dangerous failure and safe failure is no longer relevant. &#13;Also the formula for the 1oo2D was updated to include a percentage of undetected failure in the comparison between the two c\hannel architecture.</span></p></body>)/Rect[118.612 650.178 150.632 664.307]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj6107 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 6106 0 R/Rect[595.22 543.891 775.22 663.891]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj6108 0 obj<</Filter/FlateDecode/Length 12287>>stream
