endstreamendobj6114 0 obj<</Annots 6115 0 R/Contents 6118 0 R/CropBox[0 0 595.22 842]/MediaBox[0 0 595.22 842]/Parent 11463 0 R/Resources<</ExtGState<</GS0 7162 0 R>>/Font<</T1_0 10283 0 R/TT0 10280 0 R/TT1 10284 0 R/TT2 10285 0 R/TT3 10312 0 R>>/ProcSet[/PDF/Text]>>/Rotate 0/Thumb 11065 0 R/Type/Page>>endobj6115 0 obj[6116 0 R 6117 0 R]endobj6116 0 obj<</AP<</N 10407 0 R>>/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/Contents(\(600\) The changes in Tables B.1 to B.13 have arisen because in IEC 61508-6 ed1.0 the failure rate figures used in the Tables were the total failure rate of the elements with the assumption that the split between safe and dangerous was 50 % safe and 50 %\ dangerous. However, for IEC 61508-6 ed2.0 it was considered that it would be clearer to just use the dangerous failure rate for each element. Therefore, the split between dangerous failure and safe failure is no longer relevant. \rAlso the formula for th\e 1oo2D was updated to include a percentage of undetected failure in the comparison between the two channel architecture.)/CreationDate(D:20100523180718+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20100524173151+02'00')/NM(21a7a6f1-2389-4cff-a0d6-4cdf49f12182)/P 6114 0 R/Popup 6117 0 R/QuadPoints[131.401 451.851 156.321 451.851 131.401 438.553 156.321 438.553]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">\(600\)</span><span\ dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt"> The changes in Tables B.1 to B.13 have arisen because in IEC 61508-6 ed1.0 the failure rate figures used in the Tables were the </span><span dir="ltr" style="text-decoration:underline;font-size:10.0pt">total</span><spa\n dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt"> failure rate of the elements with the assumption that the split between safe and dangerous was 50 % safe and 50 % dangerous. However, for IEC 61508-6 ed2.0 it was considered that it would be clearer to just use the da\ngerous failure rate for each element. Therefore, the split between dangerous failure and safe failure is no longer relevant. &#13;Also the formula for the 1oo2D was updated to include a percentage of undetected failure in the comparison between the two c\hannel architecture.</span></p></body>)/Rect[127.851 438.138 159.871 452.267]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj6117 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 6116 0 R/Rect[595.22 331.851 775.22 451.851]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj6118 0 obj<</Filter/FlateDecode/Length 13233>>stream
