endstreamendobj6119 0 obj<</Annots 6120 0 R/Contents 6123 0 R/CropBox[0 0 595.22 842]/MediaBox[0 0 595.22 842]/Parent 11463 0 R/Resources<</ExtGState<</GS0 7162 0 R>>/Font<</C2_0 10412 0 R/T1_0 10283 0 R/TT0 10280 0 R/TT1 10284 0 R/TT2 10312 0 R/TT3 10285 0 R>>/ProcSet[/PDF/Text]>>/Rotate 0/Thumb 11066 0 R/Type/Page>>endobj6120 0 obj[6121 0 R 6122 0 R]endobj6121 0 obj<</AP<</N 10409 0 R>>/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/Contents(\(600\) The changes in Tables B.1 to B.13 have arisen because in IEC 61508-6 ed1.0 the failure rate figures used in the Tables were the total failure rate of the elements with the assumption that the split between safe and dangerous was 50 % safe and 50 %\ dangerous. However, for IEC 61508-6 ed2.0 it was considered that it would be clearer to just use the dangerous failure rate for each element. Therefore, the split between dangerous failure and safe failure is no longer relevant. \rAlso the formula for th\e 1oo2D was updated to include a percentage of undetected failure in the comparison between the two channel architecture.)/CreationDate(D:20100523180728+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20100524173151+02'00')/NM(2a922646-2ec2-47d7-8382-e16c4fa8906f)/P 6119 0 R/Popup 6122 0 R/QuadPoints[138.121 318.411 163.041 318.411 138.121 305.113 163.041 305.113]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">\(600\)</span><span\ dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt"> The changes in Tables B.1 to B.13 have arisen because in IEC 61508-6 ed1.0 the failure rate figures used in the Tables were the </span><span dir="ltr" style="text-decoration:underline;font-size:10.0pt">total</span><spa\n dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt"> failure rate of the elements with the assumption that the split between safe and dangerous was 50 % safe and 50 % dangerous. However, for IEC 61508-6 ed2.0 it was considered that it would be clearer to just use the da\ngerous failure rate for each element. Therefore, the split between dangerous failure and safe failure is no longer relevant. &#13;Also the formula for the 1oo2D was updated to include a percentage of undetected failure in the comparison between the two c\hannel architecture.</span></p></body>)/Rect[134.571 304.698 166.591 318.827]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj6122 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 6121 0 R/Rect[595.22 198.411 775.22 318.411]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj6123 0 obj<</Filter/FlateDecode/Length 12917>>stream
