6 ed2.0 it was considered that it would be clearer to just use the da\ngerous failure rate for each element. Therefore, the split between dangerous failure and safe failure is no longer relevant. &#13;Also the formula for the 1oo2D was updated to include a percentage of undetected failure in the comparison between the two c\hannel architecture.</span></p></body>)/Rect[121.832 744.119 153.928 758.337]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj6131 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 6130 0 R/Rect[595.22 637.918 775.22 757.918]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj6132 0 obj<</AP<</N 10420 0 R>>/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/Contents(\(600\) The changes in Tables B.1 to B.13 have arisen because in IEC 61508-6 ed1.0 the failure rate figures used in the Tables were the total failure rate of the elements with the assumption that the split between safe and dangerous was 50 % safe and 50 %\ dangerous. However, for IEC 61508-6 ed2.0 it was considered that it would be clearer to just use the dangerous failure rate for each element. Therefore, the split between dangerous failure and safe failure is no longer relevant. \rAlso the formula for th\e 1oo2D was updated to include a percentage of undetected failure in the comparison between the two channel architecture.)/CreationDate(D:20100523180741+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20100524173204+02'00')/NM(157c2074-ca97-4efd-a7e6-9ab3d795eeb9)/P 6128 0 R/Popup 6133 0 R/QuadPoints[130.33 588.95 155.282 588.95 130.33 575.569 155.282 575.569]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">\(600\)</span><span\ dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt"> The changes in Tables B.1 to B.13 have arisen because in IEC 61508-6 ed1.0 the failure rate figures used in the Tables were the </span><span dir="ltr" style="text-decoration:underline;font-size:10.0pt">total</span><spa\n dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt"> failure rate of the elements with the assumption that the split between safe and dangerous was 50 % safe and 50 % dangerous. However, for IEC 61508-6 ed2.0 it was considered that it would be clearer to just use the da\ngerous failure rate for each element. Therefore, the split between dangerous failure and safe failure is no longer relevant. &#13;Also the formula for the 1oo2D was updated to include a percentage of undetected failure in the comparison between the two c\hannel architecture.</span></p></body>)/Rect[126.758 575.151 158.854 589.368]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj6133 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 6132 0 R/Rect[595.22 468.95 775.22 588.95]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj6134 0 obj<</AP<</N 10418 0 R>>/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/Contents(\(600\) The changes in Tables B.1 to B.13 have arisen because in IEC 61508-6 ed1.0 the failure rate figures used in the Tables were the total failure rate of the elements with the assumption that the split between safe and dangerous was 50 % safe and 50 %\ dangerous. However, for IEC 61508-6 ed2.0 it was considered that it would be clearer to just use the dangerous failure rate for each element. Therefore, the split between dangerous failure and safe failure is no longer relevant. \rAlso the formula for th\e 1oo2D was updated to include a percentage of undetected failure in the comparison between the two channel architecture.)/CreationDate(D:20100523180747+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20100524173204+02'00')/NM(4f297751-48e3-48d1-bfc2-9e5ae47d97b1)/P 6128 0 R/Popup 6135 0 R/QuadPoints[145.812 419.991 170.764 419.991 145.812 406.61 170.764 406.61]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">\(600\)</span><span\ dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt"> The changes in Tables B.1 to B.13 have arisen because in IEC 61508-6 ed1.0 the failure rate figures used in the Tables were the </span><span dir="ltr" style="text-decoration:underline;font-size:10.0pt">total</span><spa\n dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt"> failure rate of the elements with the assumption that the split between safe and dangerous was 50 % safe and 50 % dangerous. However, for IEC 61508-6 ed2.0 it was considered that it would be clearer to just use the da\ngerous failure rate for each element. Therefore, the split between dangerous failure and safe failure is no longer relevant. &#13;Also the formula for the 1oo2D was updated to include a percentage of undetected failure in the comparison between the two c\hannel architecture.</span></p></body>)/Rect[142.24 406.192 174.336 420.409]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj6135 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 6134 0 R/Rect[595.22 299.991 775.22 419.991]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj6136 0 obj<</Filter/FlateDecode/Length 5445>>stream
