a:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">\(4\)</span><span d\ir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt"> The revised wording provides a more precise technical description of the intended requirement.</span></p></body>)/Rect[246.523 339.218 267.297 355.863]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj6144 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 6143 0 R/Rect[595.22 235.373 775.22 355.373]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj6145 0 obj<</AP<</N 10429 0 R>>/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/Contents(\(4\) The revised wording provides a more precise technical description of the intended requirement.)/CreationDate(D:20100523163511+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20100524173204+02'00')/NM(14a08668-6e9b-428e-9d7b-112b2e944869)/P 6139 0 R/Popup 6146 0 R/QuadPoints[103.2 255.657 116.239 255.657 103.2 242.356 116.239 242.356]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">\(4\)</span><span d\ir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt"> The revised wording provides a more precise technical description of the intended requirement.</span></p></body>)/Rect[99.6492 241.94 119.79 256.072]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj6146 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 6145 0 R/Rect[595.22 135.657 775.22 255.657]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj6147 0 obj<</AP<</N 10433 0 R>>/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/Contents(\(600\) The changes in Tables B.1 to B.13 have arisen because in IEC 61508-6 ed1.0 the failure rate figures used in the Tables were the total failure rate of the elements with the assumption that the split between safe and dangerous was 50 % safe and 50 %\ dangerous. However, for IEC 61508-6 ed2.0 it was considered that it would be clearer to just use the dangerous failure rate for each element. Therefore, the split between dangerous failure and safe failure is no longer relevant. \rAlso the formula for th\e 1oo2D was updated to include a percentage of undetected failure in the comparison between the two channel architecture.)/CreationDate(D:20100523180755+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20100524173204+02'00')/NM(67791cb4-e8d2-447b-b33b-e9f3f9142e1d)/P 6139 0 R/Popup 6148 0 R/QuadPoints[210.962 593.453 235.887 593.453 210.962 580.153 235.887 580.153]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">\(600\)</span><span\ dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt"> The changes in Tables B.1 to B.13 have arisen because in IEC 61508-6 ed1.0 the failure rate figures used in the Tables were the </span><span dir="ltr" style="text-decoration:underline;font-size:10.0pt">total</span><spa\n dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt"> failure rate of the elements with the assumption that the split between safe and dangerous was 50 % safe and 50 % dangerous. However, for IEC 61508-6 ed2.0 it was considered that it would be clearer to just use the da\ngerous failure rate for each element. Therefore, the split between dangerous failure and safe failure is no longer relevant. &#13;Also the formula for the 1oo2D was updated to include a percentage of undetected failure in the comparison between the two c\hannel architecture.</span></p></body>)/Rect[207.411 579.737 239.438 593.869]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj6148 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 6147 0 R/Rect[595.22 473.453 775.22 593.453]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj6149 0 obj<</Filter/FlateDecode/Length 7263>>stream
