e comparison between the two channel architecture.)/CreationDate(D:20100523180811+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20100524173204+02'00')/NM(693bc489-b5ab-4909-a9ed-59b4afb21c97)/P 6161 0 R/Popup 6166 0 R/QuadPoints[140.881 669.519 165.802 669.519 140.881 656.237 165.802 656.237]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">\(600\)</span><span\ dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt"> The changes in Tables B.1 to B.13 have arisen because in IEC 61508-6 ed1.0 the failure rate figures used in the Tables were the </span><span dir="ltr" style="text-decoration:underline;font-size:10.0pt">total</span><spa\n dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt"> failure rate of the elements with the assumption that the split between safe and dangerous was 50 % safe and 50 % dangerous. However, for IEC 61508-6 ed2.0 it was considered that it would be clearer to just use the da\ngerous failure rate for each element. Therefore, the split between dangerous failure and safe failure is no longer relevant. &#13;Also the formula for the 1oo2D was updated to include a percentage of undetected failure in the comparison between the two c\hannel architecture.</span></p></body>)/Rect[137.336 655.822 169.348 669.934]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj6166 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 6165 0 R/Rect[595.22 549.519 775.22 669.519]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj6167 0 obj<</Filter/FlateDecode/Length 16391>>stream
