e comparison between the two channel architecture.)/CreationDate(D:20100523180819+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20100524173204+02'00')/NM(b4ab5a37-2dce-4a42-bb6f-1763fa6eda60)/P 6168 0 R/Popup 6173 0 R/QuadPoints[140.881 370.719 165.802 370.719 140.881 357.437 165.802 357.437]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">\(600\)</span><span\ dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt"> The changes in Tables B.1 to B.13 have arisen because in IEC 61508-6 ed1.0 the failure rate figures used in the Tables were the </span><span dir="ltr" style="text-decoration:underline;font-size:10.0pt">total</span><spa\n dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt"> failure rate of the elements with the assumption that the split between safe and dangerous was 50 % safe and 50 % dangerous. However, for IEC 61508-6 ed2.0 it was considered that it would be clearer to just use the da\ngerous failure rate for each element. Therefore, the split between dangerous failure and safe failure is no longer relevant. &#13;Also the formula for the 1oo2D was updated to include a percentage of undetected failure in the comparison between the two c\hannel architecture.</span></p></body>)/Rect[137.336 357.022 169.348 371.134]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj6173 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 6172 0 R/Rect[595.22 250.719 775.22 370.719]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj6174 0 obj<</Filter/FlateDecode/Length 15340>>stream
