between the two channel architecture.)/CreationDate(D:20100523180828+02'00')/F 132/M(D:20100524173204+02'00')/NM(87b72306-077c-4969-81a4-7a85e29f15a5)/P 6177 0 R/Popup 6182 0 R/QuadPoints[140.881 757.839 165.802 757.839 140.881 744.557 165.802 744.557]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-weight:bold">\(600\)</span><span\ dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt"> The changes in Tables B.1 to B.13 have arisen because in IEC 61508-6 ed1.0 the failure rate figures used in the Tables were the </span><span dir="ltr" style="text-decoration:underline;font-size:10.0pt">total</span><spa\n dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt"> failure rate of the elements with the assumption that the split between safe and dangerous was 50 % safe and 50 % dangerous. However, for IEC 61508-6 ed2.0 it was considered that it would be clearer to just use the da\ngerous failure rate for each element. Therefore, the split between dangerous failure and safe failure is no longer relevant. &#13;Also the formula for the 1oo2D was updated to include a percentage of undetected failure in the comparison between the two c\hannel architecture.</span></p></body>)/Rect[137.336 744.142 169.348 758.254]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>endobj6182 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 6181 0 R/Rect[595.22 637.839 775.22 757.839]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj6183 0 obj<</Filter/FlateDecode/Length 15993>>stream
